(12, 'Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio: Girl from Kole District Shines with Five Titles at Miss Universe Uganda 2026', 'kimberly-jael-aremo-acio-girl-from-kole-district-shines-with-five-titles-at-miss-universe-uganda-2026', 'The 19-year-old from Kole District made history by winning five prestigious titles at the inaugural Miss Universe Uganda competition, including First Runner-Up, Miss Afrikana, Wellness Queen, and People\'s Choice.', '<p><strong>Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio</strong> from Kole District captivated the audience and judges at the <strong>Imperial Royale Hotel in Kampala</strong> on Saturday night, demonstrating remarkable grace, intelligence, and stage presence throughout the competition. Her exceptional performance earned her an unprecedented <strong>five prestigious titles</strong>, making her the most decorated contestant of the inaugural <strong>Miss Universe Uganda</strong> grand finale.</p><ol><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span><strong>1st Runner Up</strong> - Miss Universe Uganda 2026</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span><strong>Miss Afrikana</strong> </li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span><strong>Wellness Queen</strong> - Health and wellness advocacy</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span><strong>People\'s Choice</strong> - Public favorite with 60,000+ votes</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span><strong>Miss Universe Kole</strong> - District representative</li></ol><h2><strong>A Night of History and Achievement</strong></h2><p>Mitchelle Daka from Budaka district was crowned the first Miss Universe Uganda, making history as the country\'s debut representative at the international Miss Universe competition. Daka, a 29-year-old model and entrepreneur, won a grand prize of Shs 24 million and a car.</p><p>Kimberly\'s journey to the top was nothing short of remarkable. She had already captured national attention as the winner of the People\'s Choice Award, securing nearly 60,000 verified votes from the public. Her advocacy work, particularly her commitment to youth empowerment and mentoring young people, resonated deeply with audiences across Uganda.</p><h2><strong>A Daughter of Otikokin Clan Honored</strong></h2><p>In attendance at the prestigious event was <strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong>, the Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, who expressed pride in Kimberly\'s outstanding achievement. Minister Engola, who has been actively involved in government relief efforts for Karamoja, took time to celebrate this moment of pride for the Otikokin clan and the people of Lango.</p><p>Kimberly\'s performance was described as \"truly amazing\" by those who witnessed it, showcasing not just beauty but intelligence, poise, and a deep commitment to community service. Her journey from bullying survivor to youth advocate and national pageant star has been an inspiration to many across the country.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/1490ad9c4e34bc71.jpeg\"></p><h2><strong>Looking Ahead</strong></h2><p>Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio now represents Kole District and the Lango region as the first runner-up in this historic competition. The winner, Mitchelle Daka, will go on to represent Uganda at the 75th Miss Universe pageant in San Juan, Puerto Rico, from November 8-24, 2026.</p><p>The Otikokin clan and the people of Kole District have every reason to celebrate their daughter\'s remarkable achievement on the national stage.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/75909cbd8b5be78f.jpeg\"></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/7e39675209b995fc.jpeg', 'Queen Kimberly Jael Acio Aremo', 12, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 952, '2026-08-02 07:46:10', '2026-09-02 19:52:06', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(14, 'Mitchelle Daka Crowned Inaugural Miss Universe Uganda 2026', 'mitchelle-daka-crowned-inaugural-miss-universe-uganda-2026-2', '29-year-old model and philanthropist Mitchelle Daka made history on August 1, 2026, becoming the first-ever Miss Universe Uganda at a spectacular grand finale …', '<p>29-year-old model and philanthropist Mitchelle Daka made history on August 1, 2026, becoming the first-ever Miss Universe Uganda at a spectacular grand finale held at the Imperial Royale Hotel in Kampala.</p><h3>A Historic Victory</h3><p>Daka, who represented Budaka District in eastern Uganda, delivered a flawless performance across the evening wear, swimwear, and final Q&amp;A rounds to clinch the top title. Her composure and articulation during the judges\' intelligence rounds sealed her historic victory .</p><p>The winner drove away with a brand-new Toyota Wish as part of her prize package .</p><h3>A Queen of Many Titles</h3><p>In addition to the inaugural crown, Daka was also named the Multimedia Queen of the Journey Award winner, recognizing her strong digital presence, storytelling, and public engagement throughout the multi-week national campaign .</p><h3>About Mitchelle Daka</h3><p>At 29, Daka is a fashion model, podcaster, digital content creator, and philanthropist .</p><ol><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Advocacy: Her platform focuses on mental health and emotional awareness, nurturing self-aware, resilient youth across Ugandan communities .</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Lifestyle: She is an active fitness enthusiast, reader, and media creator who built her brand around fashion and community service long before stepping onto the national stage .</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Global Perspective: She has lived in Uganda, Kenya, and South Africa, bringing a rich understanding of diverse cultures to her role .</li></ol><p><strong>The Road to Puerto Rico</strong></p><p>As the newly crowned queen, Daka will now carry Uganda\'s flag to the 75th Miss Universe global pageant in San Juan, Puerto Rico, later this year—marking Uganda\'s debut on the Miss Universe stage .</p><p><strong>A Night of Celebration</strong></p><p>The grand finale was attended by the Minister of Energy and Mineral Development, Hon. Ruth Nankabirwa, Hon Sam Engola Minister for Relief Disaster Preparedness and Refugess (Kimberly\'s clan chief) alongside international guest Jean Ojiro (Miss Universe Kenya 2021) . The evening featured performances from top Ugandan artists including Maurice Kirya, Lilian Mbabazi, Bien (former Sauti Sol frontman), Karole Kasita, and Joshua Baraka .</p><p><strong>The Inaugural Year</strong></p><p>Organized under the executive direction of Joram Muzira Job (Joram Model Management), the event delivered a top-tier production that lived up to its international billing . Uganda officially steps into the global Miss Universe arena with a solid representative in Mitchelle Daka, backed by an exceptional court of young leaders ready to elevate the country\'s brand worldwide . Congratulations, Mitchelle Daka! Uganda is behind you as you prepare to take on the world at Miss Universe 2026.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/31c773beb5e7326e.jpg', 'Photo Credit: Kampala Edge Times - Miss Universe 2026 1st and 2nd Runners Up', 12, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 123, '2026-08-02 08:49:27', '2026-09-02 23:11:55', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(17, 'Luo Legacy Dinner Set for August 8 2026 at Sheraton Kampala', 'luo-legacy-dinner-set-for-august-8-2026-at-sheraton-kampala-3', 'The Luo community in Uganda is preparing for a landmark celebration of culture, unity, and heritage at the prestigious Sheraton Kampala Hotel on Saturday, August 8.', '<h2><strong>A Night of Culture and Celebration</strong></h2><p>The highly anticipated <strong>Luo Legacy Dinner</strong> promises to be more than just a social gathering—it is envisioned as a pivotal moment for the community to unite and shape a lasting legacy for future generations.</p><blockquote><em>This is more than a dinner—it is a celebration of who we are as Luo people, our rich culture, our history, and the legacy we want to leave - Robert Okodia </em>Sub-Region Coordinator and event spearhead</blockquote><p>The evening will bring together a diverse cross-section of the Luo community, including cultural leaders who will preside over traditions and cultural presentations, professionals sharing their expertise and networking with peers, business people exploring investment opportunities, and youth engaging in mentorship and inspiration.</p><h3><strong>Highlights of the Evening</strong></h3><ol><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Traditional Food - Authentic Luo cuisine</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Cultural Artifacts - Showcasing rich heritage</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Traditional Performances - Music and dance</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Special Tributes - Honoring outstanding community contributors</li></ol><h3><strong>A Call for Unity</strong></h3><p>Robert Okodia extended a special invitation to both Luos and friends of the community, emphasizing the core message of the event: <strong>preserving cultural heritage while embracing innovation and development</strong>.</p><blockquote><em>\"The Luo Legacy Dinner is a chance for us to unite, inspire one another, and build a stronger future for our children. I encourage everyone—whether you are Luo or a friend of the Luo community—to join us.\"</em></blockquote><h3><strong>A Broader Movement</strong></h3><p>The dinner comes at a time when the preservation of cultural heritage has been a focal point for the broader Luo community across East Africa. Recent high-profile events, such as the <strong>Piny Luo Festival in Siaya County</strong>, have similarly aimed to promote unity, peace, and the celebration of shared roots among various Luo groups across the region. The Luo Legacy Dinner echoes these sentiments, seeking to strengthen bonds and cultural identity within the Ugandan context.</p><h3><strong>Join the Celebration</strong></h3><p>All roads will lead to the Sheraton Kampala Hotel on August 8 for this prestigious event. Guests are encouraged to come dressed elegantly and prepare for an evening of celebration, purpose, and unity. Let us come together to celebrate our heritage, honor our leaders, and build a stronger future for generations to come. </p><p>For reservations and inquiries regarding the Luo Legacy Dinner, please contact the organizing team on 0782 682 239, 0778 145 842, or 0780 207 164</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/c3ab2cdcde73a830.png', 'The Luo Legacy Dinner 2026', 8, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 115, '2026-08-03 11:12:11', '2026-09-03 05:01:57', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(18, 'Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio Ranks Top 3 Most Searched Women in Uganda Right Now on Internet', 'kimberly-jael-aremo-acio-ranks-top-3-most-searched-women-in-uganda-right-now-on-internet', '#1: Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio – The Undisputed Queen of Uganda\'s InternetAccording to internet search trends across Uganda, Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio has emerged…', '<h3><br></h3><h3><strong>#1: Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio – The Undisputed Queen of Uganda\'s Internet</strong></h3><p><span>According to internet search trends across Uganda, Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio has emerged as the most searched and talked-about woman in the country, topping the charts and dominating headlines for the past week. The 19-year-old from Kole District has become a household name after her stunning performance at the inaugural Miss Universe Uganda 2026. She didn\'t just walk away as 1st Runner-Up—she left with an impressive collection of five titles, everyone expected her to be the winner of the Miss Universe Uganda 2026</span></p><h3><strong>Why She\'s #1</strong></h3><p><span>Kimberly\'s combination of youth, beauty, intelligence, and her underdog story resonates most with Ugandans. The main reason is that everyone expected her to win in all aspects as she was loved across the media hence becoming the most talked about lady on the internet since 1 August 2026. Her journey from Kole District—a small district in northern Uganda—to the national stage has inspired countless young people.</span></p><p><span>Her five titles, including the People\'s Choice Award with nearly 60,000 votes, demonstrate her undeniable connection with the public. She is not just a beauty queen; she is a symbol of hope for young Ugandans who dare to dream big.</span></p><p><span>Her character was further highlighted when she reportedly declined a personal cash offer and instead redirected the donation to the Karamoja hunger relief drive—an act that showcased her community-first values and selfless leadership.</span></p><p><span> </span></p><h3><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/b01dfcd5ba3adc67.png\"></h3><h3><br></h3><h3><strong>#2: Mitchelle Daka – The History Maker</strong></h3><p><span>At 29, Mitchelle Daka made history as the first-ever Miss Universe Uganda. The Budaka district representative delivered a flawless performance across the evening wear, swimwear, and final Q&amp;A rounds, impressing both the judges and the audience.</span></p><p><strong>Beyond the crown</strong><span>, she drives away with a brand-new </span><strong>Toyota Wish</strong><span> and carries the hopes of a nation as she prepares to represent Uganda at the </span><strong>75th Miss Universe pageant</strong><span> in San Juan, Puerto Rico. What sets Daka apart is her powerful advocacy for </span><strong>mental health and emotional awareness</strong><span>—a cause born from personal tragedy. Daka co-founded the Karabo Mokoena Foundation and has since worked tirelessly to support abused women and children. Her composure, articulation, and depth during the judges\' intelligence rounds sealed her historic victory, and she now stands as a symbol of resilience and purpose for young Ugandans.</span></p><h3><br></h3><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/a56afecffaa0b65a.png\"></p><h3><strong>#3: Alicia – The Mysterious New Bride</strong></h3><p><span>One of the most talked-about woman on Ugandan social media right now is </span><strong>Alicia</strong><span>, the new wife of popular singer </span><strong>A Pass</strong><span>.</span></p><p><span>The 36-year-old \"Wuuyo\" hitmaker, who once joked he would never marry until age 70, shocked the nation on </span><strong>August 1, 2026</strong><span>, when he announced his secret traditional wedding with a simple caption: </span><em>\"Married\" </em></p><p><span>Alicia, who has largely stayed out of the spotlight, is now the subject of intense curiosity. Her identity remains something of a mystery—public reporting has so far identified her only by her first name, with no widely published details yet on her profession, background, or family.</span></p><p><span>What is known is that the relationship was not a sudden reveal. In an interview months before the wedding, A Pass had already confirmed he was in a serious relationship and hinted at planning a traditional ceremony.</span></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/7c534a77ff79dbbd.jpeg', 'Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio at the Miss Universe Pagentry', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 0, '2026-08-03 14:04:23', '2026-08-03 14:04:23', 1, 1, 'lora'),
(21, 'Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio Ranks Top 3 Most Searched Women in Uganda Right Now on Internet', 'kimberly-jael-aremo-acio-ranks-top-3-most-searched-women-in-uganda-right-now-on-internet-4', '#1: Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio – The Undisputed Queen of Uganda\'s InternetAccording to internet search trends across Uganda, Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio has emerged…', '<h3><br></h3><h3><strong>#1: Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio – The Undisputed Queen of Uganda\'s Internet</strong></h3><p>According to internet search trends across Uganda, Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio has emerged as the most searched and talked-about woman in the country, topping the charts and dominating headlines for the past week. The 19-year-old from Kole District has become a household name after her stunning performance at the inaugural Miss Universe Uganda 2026. She didn\'t just walk away as 1st Runner-Up—she left with an impressive collection of five titles, everyone expected her to be the winner of the Miss Universe Uganda 2026</p><h3><strong>Why She\'s #1</strong></h3><p>Kimberly\'s combination of youth, beauty, intelligence, and her underdog story resonates most with Ugandans. The main reason is that everyone expected her to win in all aspects as she was loved across the media hence becoming the most talked about lady on the internet since 1 August 2026. Her journey from Kole District—a small district in northern Uganda—to the national stage has inspired countless young people.</p><p>Her five titles, including the People\'s Choice Award with nearly 60,000 votes, demonstrate her undeniable connection with the public. She is not just a beauty queen; she is a symbol of hope for young Ugandans who dare to dream big.</p><p>Her character was further highlighted when she reportedly declined a personal cash offer and instead redirected the donation to the Karamoja hunger relief drive—an act that showcased her community-first values and selfless leadership.</p><h3><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/e02672d9db695a85.png\"></h3><h3><br></h3><h3><strong>#2: Mitchelle Daka – The History Maker</strong></h3><p>At 29, Mitchelle Daka made history as the first-ever Miss Universe Uganda. The Budaka district representative delivered a flawless performance across the evening wear, swimwear, and final Q&amp;A rounds, impressing both the judges and the audience.</p><p><strong>Beyond the crown</strong>, she drives away with a brand-new <strong>Toyota Wish</strong> and carries the hopes of a nation as she prepares to represent Uganda at the <strong>75th Miss Universe pageant</strong> in San Juan, Puerto Rico. What sets Daka apart is her powerful advocacy for <strong>mental health and emotional awareness</strong>—a cause born from personal tragedy. Daka co-founded the Karabo Mokoena Foundation and has since worked tirelessly to support abused women and children. Her composure, articulation, and depth during the judges\' intelligence rounds sealed her historic victory, and she now stands as a symbol of resilience and purpose for young Ugandans.</p><h3><br></h3><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/a56afecffaa0b65a.png\"></p><h3><strong>#3: Alicia – The Mysterious New Bride</strong></h3><p>One of the most talked-about woman on Ugandan social media right now is <strong>Alicia</strong>, the new wife of popular singer <strong>A Pass</strong>.</p><p>The 36-year-old \"Wuuyo\" hitmaker, who once joked he would never marry until age 70, shocked the nation on <strong>August 1, 2026</strong>, when he announced his secret traditional wedding with a simple caption: <em>\"Married\" </em></p><p>Alicia, who has largely stayed out of the spotlight, is now the subject of intense curiosity. Her identity remains something of a mystery—public reporting has so far identified her only by her first name, with no widely published details yet on her profession, background, or family.</p><p>What is known is that the relationship was not a sudden reveal. In an interview months before the wedding, A Pass had already confirmed he was in a serious relationship and hinted at planning a traditional ceremony.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/6c5ed82c34b94b28.png', 'Kimberly Jael Aremo Acio at the Miss Universe Pagentry', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 226, '2026-08-03 14:13:24', '2026-09-03 08:03:05', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(22, 'Hon. Sam Engola chairs capacity building workshop for members of parliament on Uganda\'s refugee response frameworks', 'hon-sam-engola-chairs-capacity-building-workshop-for-members-of-parliament-on-uganda-s-refugee-response-frameworks', 'KAMPALA – The Capacity Building Workshop for Members of Parliament on Uganda\'s Refugee Response Frameworks officially opened today at Sheraton Kampala Hotel, w…', '<p><strong>KAMPALA –</strong><span> The Capacity Building Workshop for Members of Parliament on Uganda\'s Refugee Response Frameworks officially opened today at Sheraton Kampala Hotel, with </span><strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong><span>, Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, chairing the two-day event. <img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/59a0306af9ca520f.jpeg\"></span></p><p><span>The workshop, organized by the Office of the Prime Minister, the Parliamentary Forum on Refugees and Internally Displaced Persons (PFR-IDPs), and the CRRF Secretariat, with support from IGAD, brings together MPs from refugee-hosting districts, Government officials, and partners including UNHCR</span></p><p><span>Uganda currently hosts over </span><strong>2 million refugees</strong><span>—the largest refugee population in Africa and the third largest in the world. With refugees primarily from South Sudan, DR Congo, and other neighbouring countries, the pressure on refugee-hosting districts continues to grow.</span></p><p><span>Speaking as Chair of the workshop, </span><strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong><span> emphasized the importance of equipping MPs with the knowledge and tools to effectively oversee and support Uganda\'s refugee response.</span></p><blockquote><em>\"This workshop is about ensuring that Parliament understands its critical role in sustaining Uganda\'s progressive refugee policy. We must bridge the gap between humanitarian assistance and long-term development, and Parliament is central to that effort,\"</em><span> Engola said.</span></blockquote><p><span>The </span><strong>Rt. Hon. Deputy Speaker of Parliament, Thomas Tayebwa</strong><span>, delivered the keynote address, commending Uganda\'s transition from a refugee-producing country to a refugee-hosting country—and one of the best in the world.</span></p><p><span>He thanked Hon. Sam Engola for his exceptional work in disaster response and food relief, and assured that Parliament will give all the necessary support to sustain the refugee response.</span></p><blockquote><em>\"Let us treat refugees as our own people because we are one people,\"</em><span> the Deputy Speaker said, urging MPs to represent refugees in their communities and advocate for adequate budgetary support.</span></blockquote><p><span>The conclusion of Day One centered on a robust discussion in which MPs from refugee-hosting districts shared their valuable inputs, drawing from their firsthand experiences and the realities on the ground. MPs highlighted pressing challenges, including resource constraints, pressure on social services, and the need for stronger coordination. The session concluded with a commitment by the technical team to consolidate the inputs, develop actionable steps, and ensure that the concerns raised are reflected in policy and budgetary decisions moving forward.</span></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/2c80ec37e03e1880.jpeg\"></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/f4f64c0cb1a80f1e.jpeg', 'Hon Sam Engola', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 0, '2026-08-05 15:37:52', '2026-08-05 15:37:52', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(23, 'Hon. Sam Engola chairs capacity building workshop for members of parliament on Uganda\'s refugee response frameworks', 'hon-sam-engola-chairs-capacity-building-workshop-for-members-of-parliament-on-uganda-s-refugee-response-frameworks-2', 'KAMPALA – The Capacity Building Workshop for Members of Parliament on Uganda\'s Refugee Response Frameworks officially opened today at Sheraton Kampala Hotel, w…', '<p><strong>KAMPALA –</strong> The Capacity Building Workshop for Members of Parliament on Uganda\'s Refugee Response Frameworks officially opened today at Sheraton Kampala Hotel, with <strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong>, Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, chairing the two-day event. <img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/59a0306af9ca520f.jpeg\"></p><p>The workshop, organized by the Office of the Prime Minister, the Parliamentary Forum on Refugees and Internally Displaced Persons (PFR-IDPs), and the CRRF Secretariat, with support from IGAD, brings together MPs from refugee-hosting districts, Government officials, and partners including UNHCR</p><p>Uganda currently hosts over <strong>2 million refugees</strong>—the largest refugee population in Africa and the third largest in the world. With refugees primarily from South Sudan, DR Congo, and other neighbouring countries, the pressure on refugee-hosting districts continues to grow.</p><p>Speaking as Chair of the workshop, <strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong> emphasized the importance of equipping MPs with the knowledge and tools to effectively oversee and support Uganda\'s refugee response.</p><blockquote><em>\"This workshop is about ensuring that Parliament understands its critical role in sustaining Uganda\'s progressive refugee policy. We must bridge the gap between humanitarian assistance and long-term development, and Parliament is central to that effort,\"</em> Engola said.</blockquote><p>The <strong>Rt. Hon. Deputy Speaker of Parliament, Thomas Tayebwa</strong>, delivered the keynote address, commending Uganda\'s transition from a refugee-producing country to a refugee-hosting country—and one of the best in the world.</p><p>He thanked Hon. Sam Engola for his exceptional work in disaster response and food relief, and assured that Parliament will give all the necessary support to sustain the refugee response.</p><blockquote><em>\"Let us treat refugees as our own people because we are one people,\"</em> the Deputy Speaker said, urging MPs to represent refugees in their communities and advocate for adequate budgetary support.</blockquote><p>The conclusion of Day One centered on a robust discussion in which MPs from refugee-hosting districts shared their valuable inputs, drawing from their firsthand experiences and the realities on the ground. MPs highlighted pressing challenges, including resource constraints, pressure on social services, and the need for stronger coordination. The session concluded with a commitment by the technical team to consolidate the inputs, develop actionable steps, and ensure that the concerns raised are reflected in policy and budgetary decisions moving forward.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/2c80ec37e03e1880.jpeg\"></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/beddc4fd6b94fdbe.jpeg', 'Hon Sam Engola', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 61, '2026-08-05 15:38:25', '2026-09-01 12:35:41', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(24, 'Hon. Andrew Oulanyah The Chairperson of Parliament\'s Committee on ICT and National Guidance Calls for Bold Digital Transformation in Uganda', 'hon-andrew-oulanyah-the-chairperson-of-parliament-s-committee-on-ict-and-national-guidance-calls-for-bold-digital-transformation-in-uganda', 'Hon. Andrew Oulanyah, has sounded a clarion call for Uganda\'s digital evolution, urging members to champion the digitisation of government services, stronger d…', '<p><strong>Hon. Andrew Oulanyah,</strong> has sounded a clarion call for Uganda\'s digital evolution, urging members to champion the digitisation of government services, stronger data protection, and robust intellectual property enforcement.</p><p>Speaking at the committee\'s two-day induction, Oulanyah emphasized the need to decentralise innovation hubs, expand affordable broadband access, and strengthen oversight of national ICT programmes—ensuring technology benefits Ugandans in every corner of the country.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/94ae7b6aa93f1899.jpeg\"></p><p>Hon. Oulanyah outlined five key priorities for Uganda\'s digital transformation:</p><ol><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>The digitisation of government services for efficient and transparent public service delivery.</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Stronger data protection to safeguard citizens\' privacy and security.</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Intellectual property enforcement to protect innovation and creators\' rights</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>Decentralised innovation hubs to empower local talent and entrepreneurship</li><li><span class=\"ql-ui\"></span>And affordable broadband access to bridge the digital divide across Uganda.</li></ol>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/465325dade41af6f.jpeg', NULL, 7, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 36, '2026-08-10 10:26:32', '2026-09-01 12:35:42', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(25, 'Trump Claims Secret Service Moved Him from Air Force One Due to Security Threat', 'trump-claims-secret-service-moved-him-from-air-force-one-due-to-security-threat', 'President Donald Trump stated he was moved to a different aircraft from Air Force One last month over a security threat, a move he downplayed.', '<p><em>This article is based on reporting by <a href=\"https://www.ctinsider.com/news/politics/article/the-latest-trump-says-he-was-taken-off-air-force-22384900.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CT Insider</a>.</em></p><h2><br></h2><h2>Trump Claims Secret Service Moved Him from Air Force One Due to Security Threat</h2><p>President Donald Trump has stated that he was moved from Air Force One last month due to a security threat, according to reporting by CT Insider. Trump claimed that the Secret Service and military wanted him on a \"different plane\" after a trip in Turkey, though he insisted the threat did not scare him.</p><p>CT Insider reports that Trump downplayed the unusual nature of the situation, which involved him allegedly using an airport catering container to board another plane while Air Force One served as a decoy. He also reportedly minimized the risks to the White House officials, security personnel, and reporters who remained on the original aircraft.</p><p>\"They wanted me to go on a different flight, different plane,\" Trump told reporters, as cited by CT Insider. \"I guess there was a threat out there. I didn’t really ask too much about it. I get a lot of threats.\" The report also touched on other political news, including the Minnesota Democratic Senate primary where Lt. Gov. Peggy Flanagan, a progressive, defeated centrist U.S. Rep. Angie Craig. Additionally, CT Insider noted that U.S. inflation showed a pause last month, though higher costs persist for consumers, with prices rising 3.4% in July from a year ago.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/057d845f9643213f.webp', 'President Donald Trump boards Air Force One at Cleveland Hopkins International Airport in Cleveland, Tuesday, Aug. 11, 2026.', 12, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 16, '2026-08-12 13:10:51', '2026-09-02 17:49:48', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(26, 'Hon. Sam Engola Updates Parliament on Food Distribution in Karamoja Region', 'hon-sam-engola-updates-parliament-on-food-distribution-in-karamoja-region', 'The Ugandan government has initiated a large-scale relief food distribution in the Karamoja Sub-region to combat drought impacts.', '<p><span>The Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees today updated Parliament on the ongoing relief food distribution in Karamoja, confirming that the government has reached all </span><strong>313,987 affected households</strong><span> across </span><strong>480 parishes in 9 districts</strong><span>. Each household is receiving </span><strong>20kg of posho and 10kg of beans</strong><span>, covering the months of July and August 2026.</span></p><p><span>The Minister also briefed Parliament on the government\'s countrywide early warning dissemination for the upcoming El Niño season. He noted that the government is using </span><strong>local radios, barazas, schools, RDCs, and district local government structures</strong><span> to ensure every citizen receives timely information to prepare for the anticipated weather challenges.</span></p><p><span>The government remains committed to supporting communities affected by climate shocks, and the Minister assured Parliament that distribution efforts are ongoing across the sub-region. He emphasized that no household in Karamoja will be left behind as the government continues to monitor the situation and respond accordingly.</span></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/0a3702f07c47afec.jpeg', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 41, '2026-08-12 13:18:22', '2026-09-02 19:59:31', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(27, 'Questions Surround Death of Kameke SS Staff Member in Pallisa', 'questions-surround-death-of-kameke-ss-staff-member-in-pallisa', 'Pallisa District is seeking answers after a long-serving Kameke SS staff member was found dead under suspicious circumstances. Police are investigating.', '<p>Pallisa District was shaken by the discovery of the body of James Walwasa, known locally as Ekomol, on Tuesday morning. His body was found hanging from a mango tree in Ocupai village, near his home in Kameke sub-county.</p><p>Walwasa was a familiar and respected figure at Kameke Secondary School, where he had served in the security department for over 25 years. Teachers described him as a dedicated individual who also acted as an unofficial counselor for both staff and students.</p><p>The discovery was made by William Asabat, the LC1 chairperson of Ocupai village, who had spoken with Walwasa the previous evening. Asabat was heading to Walwasa\'s home to discuss community matters when he was met with sounds of mourning. Upon arrival at the scene, officials found a crowd had already gathered, which hampered initial police efforts, including the use of a sniffer dog. The District Police Commander, Patience Namara, urged residents to seek help for their problems and to allow the police to conduct their investigation.</p><p>Detectives noted several details about the body that did not align with a typical suicide by hanging. These included the absence of protruding eyes or tongue, and the rope knot being found at the front of the neck.</p><p>Due to these observations, Commander Namara ordered a postmortem examination at Pallisa General Hospital to determine the exact cause of death, emphasizing that the case was being treated as criminal.</p><p>Some relatives initially expressed concerns about the cost of a postmortem, but the LC3 Chairperson, Vincent Oluka Epokeom, intervened, and a relative agreed to cover transport expenses, allowing the examination to proceed.</p><p>Conflicting accounts have emerged regarding Walwasa\'s last hours. One resident stated Walwasa was in his work uniform and planning to report to school early, while another, speaking anonymously, suggested a domestic quarrel had occurred the previous night. </p><p>The school administration at Kameke SS expressed deep shock and grief, noting this was the second loss the institution had experienced in two months. They appealed for community prayers.</p><p>Police have stated that the official cause of death will only be confirmed once the postmortem results are released, leaving the community and school awaiting definitive answers.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/971de11b60260ad7.webp', NULL, 2, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 22, '2026-08-12 14:17:30', '2026-09-01 12:35:41', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(28, 'Hon. Angwech Pamela Engola: Lira Youth Urged to Embrace Farming and Vocational Skills for Future Security', 'lira-youth-urged-to-embrace-farming-and-vocational-skills-for-future-security', 'Hon. Angwech Pamela Engola encouraged Lira\'s youth to leverage government programs and engage in agriculture and vocational training to build wealth and secure their future.', '<p>On International Youth Day, Lira City Vice Chairperson and Youth League representative, Hon. Angwech Pamela Engola, has called upon the youth in the Lango sub-region to transform challenges into opportunities. She emphasized that the day serves as a critical reminder of the youth\'s pivotal role in Uganda\'s development trajectory.</p><p>Addressing the global theme, “Different Contexts, Common Aspirations,” Hon. Angwech highlighted the shared struggles of young people in Lira and other Least Developed Countries (LDCs). These include unemployment, the impacts of climate change, and resource limitations, all while harboring common dreams for jobs, education, and participation in decision-making processes.</p><p>With the current rainy season, Hon. Angwech specifically urged young people in Lango to actively participate in productive agriculture and income-generating activities. She pointed to government initiatives such as the Parish Development Model (PDM), NUSAF IV, and Emyooga as valuable resources that youth should utilize to foster wealth creation and self-employment.</p><p>The youth leader stressed the importance of proactive engagement, stating that young people are not just future leaders but present-day drivers of Uganda\'s transformation. She encouraged creativity and productivity, urging them to contribute hope and unity to their communities and the nation.</p><p>The commemoration of International Youth Day, established by the UN General Assembly, aims to spotlight youth issues and celebrate their societal contributions. It provides a platform for dialogue and showcases youth-led solutions for building inclusive and peaceful societies.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/456f69fa0d38a728.png', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 18, '2026-08-12 14:23:11', '2026-09-02 15:43:17', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(30, 'Prime Minister Robinah Nabbanja Briefs Media on Upcoming National Cleaning Day 29th August 2026', 'prime-minister-nabbanja-briefs-media-on-upcoming-national-cleaning-day', 'Prime Minister Robinah Nabbanja led a briefing on the upcoming National Cleaning Day, scheduled for the last Saturday of August.', '<h2>National Cleaning Day Set for August 29th</h2><p>The Rt. Hon. Prime Minister Robinah Nabbanja, alongside the Third Deputy Prime Minister and other ministers, held a media briefing this afternoon to discuss the forthcoming National Cleaning Day. The national initiative, aimed at promoting cleanliness and public health, is scheduled to take place on the last Saturday of the current month, which falls on August 29th.</p><p>The briefing included technical staff from the Office of the Prime Minister, who provided further details on the organization and objectives of the day.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/7c1e80130d59100e.jpeg', 'Photo Credit: OPM Media', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 22, '2026-08-12 14:50:38', '2026-08-31 12:53:01', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(31, 'The Northern Uganda Volleyball Association (NUVA) has launched a national referees training course in Lira City', 'nuva-kicks-off-national-referees-training-course-in-lira-city', 'The Northern Uganda Volleyball Association (NUVA) has launched a national referees training course aimed at developing officiating standards for the 2026 season.', '<p>Lira: The Northern Uganda Volleyball Association (NUVA), in collaboration with the Uganda Volleyball Federation (UVF), has officially commenced the National Referees Training Course 2026. The three-day event, held at Lavington Park in Lira City, began on Tuesday, August 11th, 2026, and is scheduled to conclude on August 13th.  A total of 32 participants are attending the course, representing various regions including Lango, Acholi, Karamoja, Buganda, and the media fraternity. The training aims to enhance the skills of aspiring referees and ensure quality officiating across the sport.</p><p>The course is being led by FIVB International Referee Innocent Komakech, who will conduct both theoretical and practical sessions. NUVA Chairperson Daniel Okwee officially opened the training, expressing excitement about rebuilding volleyball in the region and the potential for participants to become FIVB International Referees. Okwee stressed the importance of high-quality officiating for the growth of volleyball in Northern Uganda, urging attendees to engage seriously with the training content. Successful candidates upon completion will be certified to officiate games sanctioned by NUVA and UVF for the 2026/27 season.</p><p>NUVA serves as the regional body responsible for the development, promotion, and regulation of volleyball in Northern Uganda under the umbrella of the Uganda Volleyball Federation.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/74f5f8b5144eae43.jpg', 'The Northern Uganda Volleyball Association (NUVA)', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 26, '2026-08-12 15:08:46', '2026-09-01 03:00:11', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(32, 'Uganda calls for regional action and voluntary repatriation strategy amid rising refugee numbers and budget deficits', 'uganda-calls-for-regional-action-and-voluntary-repatriation-strategy-amid-rising-refugee-numbers-and-budget-deficits', '‎The Government of Uganda has called on neighboring countries to formulate concrete, actionable plans for the voluntary, safe, and sustainable repatriation of …', '<p>‎The Government of Uganda has called on neighboring countries to formulate concrete, actionable plans for the voluntary, safe, and sustainable repatriation of refugees to their home countries. ‎The call was made today by the Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, Hon. Sam Engola, during the opening of the JICA-OPM regional knowledge-sharing workshop on refugee and IDP responses at Fairway Hotel in Kampala.</p><p>‎</p><p>‎Organized jointly by Office of the Prime Minister (OPM) and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), the workshop brought together delegates and representatives from Burundi, Ethiopia, Kenya, Rwanda, Somalia, South Sudan, and Sudan, alongside representatives from the Embassy of Japan. </p><p>‎</p><p>‎Engola said that severe funding gaps threaten support for over 2 Million refugees warning that while emergency aid remains crucial, global humanitarian funding is steadily declining for over 2 million refugees in the country. ‎He explained that Uganda’s refugee operation is currently functioning at less than 50% of its required budget adding that despite this resource crunch, the overall number of refugees entering the country continues to rise due to increase in the number of refugees and asylum-seekers, cementing its status as one of Africa’s largest refugee-hosting nations.</p><p>‎</p><p>‎\"Emergency assistance remains important, but it is not enough on its own. We need longer-term approaches that support development, strengthen peace, and help communities recover,\" Hon. Engola emphasized.  </p><p>‎</p><p>‎To relieve growing pressure on public infrastructure, local services, and host communities, Hon. Engola stated that the government is requesting participating nations to conclude the regional engagement with actionable frameworks supporting voluntary returns to countries of origin. ‎The Minister commended Burundi as a positive model, noting that its targeted efforts have already resulted in 17,458 refugees voluntarily registering to return home.</p><p>‎Regional Context and Policy Commitment.</p><p>‎</p><p>‎The broader East, Horn of Africa, and Great Lakes regions face staggering forced displacement driven by ongoing conflicts, political instability, and climate shocks. ‎Despite these growing pressures, Engola said Uganda under the leadership of President Yoweri Kaguta Museveni has maintained an open-door refugee policy. The policy actively supports both refugees and host communities to coexist peacefully, access public services, and pursue sustainable livelihoods.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/1b2f5dc9f990632e.jpeg', 'Photo with JICA - OPM Officials at Fairway Hotel Kampala', 33, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 32, '2026-08-13 09:01:14', '2026-08-31 20:57:55', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(33, 'Energy Ministry Asks Parliament to Waive Shs2.6bn Mineral Rent Arrears Owed by Kilembe Mines', 'energy-ministry-asks-parliament-to-waive-shs2-6bn-mineral-rent-arrears-owed-by-kilembe-mines', 'The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development has asked Parliament to waive Shs2.6bn in mineral rent arrears owed by Kilembe Mines Ltd as government prepares to hand over operations to a new mining consortium.', '<p>PARLIAMENT – The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development is seeking a Shs2.6 billion tax arrears waiver for Kilembe Mines Limited as the government-owned company winds up operations to pave way for a new mining company.</p><p>Appearing before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development on Wednesday  this week, the State Minister for Minerals, Hon. Sidronius Okaasai said the amount accrued from unpaid annual mineral rents by Kilembe Mines Limited when it held the mining licence.</p><p>According to the Minister, the arrears were charged in accordance with Section 189 of the Mining and Minerals Act, Cap. 159.</p><p>The waiver request comes after government in 2025 signed a new mineral production sharing agreement with a joint company comprising:</p><p>Sarrai Group Ltd</p><p>Nile Fibreboard Ltd</p><p>Uganda National Mining Company Ltd</p><p>The consortium has been contracted for the exploration, development, production and processing of minerals at Kilembe Mines in Kasese District.</p><p>Minister Okaasai told the committee that clearing the arrears is necessary to finalize the winding up of the old Kilembe Mines Limited and allow the new investors to take over operations without legal and financial encumbrances.</p><p>The Committee is expected to scrutinize the request and make a recommendation to Parliament.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/33bba39e0d503c41.jpg', 'State Minister for Minerals Hon. Sidronius Okaasai appears before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development over Kilembe Mines tax waiver', 33, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 0, 0, '2026-08-13 16:30:39', '2026-08-13 16:30:39', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(34, 'Govt Seeks Shs2.6bn Tax Waiver for Kilembe Mines to Clear Way for New Investors.', 'govt-seeks-shs2-6bn-tax-waiver-for-kilembe-mines-to-clear-way-for-new-investors', 'The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development has asked Parliament to waive Shs2.6bn in mineral rent arrears owed by Kilembe Mines Ltd', '<p><strong>By Regina Lalam </strong></p><p><strong>PARLIAMENT – </strong>The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development is seeking a Shs2.6 billion tax arrears waiver for Kilembe Mines Limited as the government-owned company winds up operations to pave way for a new mining company.</p><p>Appearing before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development on Wednesday this week, the State Minister for Minerals, Hon. Sidronius Okaasai said the amount accrued from unpaid annual mineral rents by Kilembe Mines Limited when it held the mining licence.</p><p>According to the Minister, the arrears were charged in accordance with Section 189 of the Mining and Minerals Act, Cap. 159.</p><p>The waiver request comes after government in 2025 signed a new mineral production sharing agreement with a joint company comprising:</p><p>Sarrai Group Ltd</p><p>Nile Fibreboard Ltd</p><p>Uganda National Mining Company Ltd</p><p>The consortium has been contracted for the exploration, development, production and processing of minerals at Kilembe Mines in Kasese District.</p><p>Minister Okaasai told the committee that clearing the arrears is necessary to finalize the winding up of the old Kilembe Mines Limited and allow the new investors to take over operations without legal and financial encumbrances.</p><p>The Committee is expected to scrutinize the request and make a recommendation to Parliament.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/796722783f094fab.jpg', 'State Minister for  Energy And minerals development Hon. Sidronius Okaasai appears before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development over Kilembe Mines tax waiver', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 0, 0, '2026-08-13 17:03:03', '2026-08-13 17:21:08', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(35, 'Govt Seeks Shs2.6bn Tax Waiver for Kilembe Mines to Clear Way for New Investors.', 'govt-seeks-shs2-6bn-tax-waiver-for-kilembe-mines-to-clear-way-for-new-investors-2', 'The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development has asked Parliament to waive Shs2.6bn in mineral rent arrears owed by Kilembe Mines Ltd', '<p><strong>By Regina Lalam </strong></p><p><strong>PARLIAMENT – </strong>The Ministry of Energy and Mineral Development is seeking a Shs2.6 billion tax arrears waiver for Kilembe Mines Limited as the government-owned company winds up operations to pave way for a new mining company.</p><p>Appearing before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development on Wednesday  this week, the State Minister for Minerals, Hon. Sidronius Okaasai said the amount accrued from unpaid annual mineral rents by Kilembe Mines Limited when it held the mining licence.</p><p>According to the Minister, the arrears were charged in accordance with Section 189 of the Mining and Minerals Act, Cap. 159.</p><p>The waiver request comes after government in 2025 signed a new mineral production sharing agreement with a joint company comprising:</p><p>Sarrai Group Ltd</p><p>Nile Fibreboard Ltd</p><p>Uganda National Mining Company Ltd</p><p>The consortium has been contracted for the exploration, development, production and processing of minerals at Kilembe Mines in Kasese District.</p><p>Minister Okaasai told the committee that clearing the arrears is necessary to finalize the winding up of the old Kilembe Mines Limited and allow the new investors to take over operations without legal and financial encumbrances.</p><p>The Committee is expected to scrutinize the request and make a recommendation to Parliament.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/20ecb0c25491cf68.jpg', 'State Minister for  Energy And minerals development Hon. Sidronius Okaasai appears before the Committee on Finance, Planning and Economic Development over Kilembe Mines tax waiver', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 47, '2026-08-13 17:38:10', '2026-08-31 13:22:11', 0, 1, 'inter');
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `excerpt`, `content`, `featured_image`, `featured_image_caption`, `category_id`, `author_id`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `status`, `is_featured`, `views`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_breaking`, `reading_time`, `body_font`) VALUES
(36, 'Kwania Police Deny Brutality Allegations During Apire LC2 Polls.', 'kwania-police-deny-brutality-allegations-during-apire-lc2-polls', 'By Hillary Opio Omara KWANIA DISTRICT : Tensions between the ruling National Resistance Movement (NRM) and the opposition Uganda People’s Congress (UPC) in Kwa…', '<p><strong>By  Hillary Opio Omara </strong></p><p><strong>KWANIA DISTRICT : </strong>Tensions between the ruling National Resistance Movement (NRM) and the opposition Uganda People’s Congress (UPC) in Kwania District have escalated following a disputed LC2 election in Apire Parish,with police arresting five people over allegations of assault,malicious damage to property and incitement to violence.</p><p>The arrests followed clashes that erupted during the election of the Apire LC2 chairperson,prompting a heavy police deployment to maintain peace and order.</p><p>Speaking during a parliamentary session on Matters of National Importance yesterday,Kwania District Woman Member of Parliament Kenny Auma Lapat accused security and local government officials of allowing political tensions to interfere with the electoral process.</p><p>Auma said she had earlier raised concerns in Parliament about what she described as growing political tensions in Kwania, particularly in Apire Parish,where she alleged that individuals were being mobilised to disrupt elections.</p><p>According to Auma,UPC initially won eight polling stations,while the NRM won only three.</p><p>She alleged that the parish electoral supervisor later arrived at the polling exercise accompanied by security and political officials,including Deputy RDC Abraham Aturu,Kwania District Police Commander SP Paul Kadoogo,the NRM District Registrar and members of the NRM Workers’ League.</p><p>Auma further alleged that during the voting exercise,the Deputy RDC entered the polling area and began interfering with the process,allegedly insisting that voters should support the NRM candidate.</p><p>She called on the Minister for the Presidency to take action against the Deputy RDC, arguing that government officials should not be used to influence electoral outcomes or reverse the gains made by the UPC in Kwania.</p><p>However,Emmanuel Opio Okello,the NRM Registrar for Kwania District,dismissed Auma’s allegations,saying the NRM has not violated electoral laws.</p><p>Opio said the NRM performed strongly in the recent parish elections,winning 37 positions compared to nine won by the UPC across Kwania.</p><p>He challenged Auma to focus on development issues affecting residents instead of what he described as political allegations based on a single parish election.</p><p>Opio also pointed to challenges facing residents,including healthcare,education, roads,agricultural programmes and unemployment.</p><p>He said that,apart from Aduku Sub-county, where the NRM won five positions out of six parishes,the party had performed strongly across the district.</p><p>The North Kyoga Regional Police Commander,SP Patrick Jimmy Okema,said police were investigating allegations of violence and destruction of property arising from the Apire election.</p><p>Okema said trouble allegedly started after a group of people accused another person of interfering with the electoral process and inciting violence.</p><p>Police said two individuals,identified as Ekaa Anna and Ambrose Okello,were among those reportedly injured during the clashes.</p><p>Five Arrested Over Election Violence</p><p>Kwania District Police Commander SP Paul Kadoogo said police deployed heavily during the election to prevent further violence and urged supporters of all political parties to respect the electoral process.</p><p>Kadoogo said police arrested Otoo Samuel, 51,of Apire \"A\",who is accused of allegedly setting fire to a grass-thatched structure during the clashes.</p><p>He said Dickens Ogwal,the LC2 Area Councillor for Apire Parish,was also arrested in connection with the violence.</p><p>According to police,the clashes resulted in the destruction of several properties and injuries to four civilians and two police officers.</p><p>Kadoogo said five suspects had so far been arrested in connection with the case, including Patrick Oruru,22,of Teopok,Ebong Tom,51,of Alongomula,and Tonny Otim,22,of Angolenyanga in Apire Parish,Aduku Sub-county.</p><p>Our news desks tried to get a comments from Deputy RDC of Kwania district but it wasn\'t available at the press time.</p><p>The election results showed Moro Tom of UPC winning the Apire LC2 chairperson position with 68 vot</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/d7b4bb3987e94093.jpg', 'Security personnel deployed in Apire Parish, Kwania District during the disputed LC2 elections.', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 191, '2026-08-13 18:05:29', '2026-09-02 18:03:16', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(37, 'Residents Burnt Suspected Livestock Theft Vehicle to Ashes in Kwania,Four Arrested.', 'residents-burnt-suspected-livestock-theft-vehicle-to-ashes-in-kwania-four-arrested', 'By Hillary Opio Omara KWANIA DISTRICT - Residents of Bung in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Kwania District,reportedly set fire to a Toyota Noah vehicle suspec…', '<p><strong>By Hillary Opio Omara </strong></p><p><strong>KWANIA DISTRICT - </strong>Residents of Bung in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Kwania District,reportedly set fire to a Toyota Noah vehicle suspected of being used to transport stolen livestock,as police arrested four people in connection with the alleged theft.</p><p>The incident occurred today Thursday,August 13,2026,after residents reportedly became suspicious of the vehicle and raised an alarm over livestock allegedly loaded inside it.</p><p>Moses Amwata,the Bung LC1 Chairperson, told OromaTv that residents noticed the Toyota Noah parked in the area and decided to investigate.</p><p>According to Amwata,residents discovered livestock inside the vehicle that they suspected had been stolen.</p><p>The situation reportedly escalated,with angry residents setting the vehicle ablaze and reducing it to ashes.</p><p>Lucy Achato,a resident and livestock owner, said the alleged theft angered residents and prompted them to intervene after becoming suspicious about the animals and the vehicle.</p><p>Dorcus Wangari,the Aduku Town Council Councilor said she received a report from the Gender and Integrated Security Office (GISO) and that she visited the scene to assess the situation.</p><p>Wangari urged residents to avoid transporting livestock at night without proper documentation.</p><p>She said livestock buyers should have documents proving ownership and showing where the animals were legally purchased.</p><p>“People should not move livestock at night without documents showing that they legally bought the animals,” Wangari said.</p><p>Kwania District Police Commander SP Kadoogo Paul confirmed that police received a report on August 13,2026, concerning a Toyota Noah registration number UAP 736K,which was allegedly being used to transport suspected stolen livestock.</p><p>He said police intervened and arrested the driver together with three other people who were inside the vehicle.</p><p>Geoffrey Okello,the GISO of Aduku Town Council,said preliminary information indicates that some of the livestock allegedly involved in the incident originated from Bala in Kole District and Akalo,among other areas.</p><p>The suspects arrested include Emmanuel Opio,a resident of Adyeda Trading Centre in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Opio Ashan,also known as Murefo,a resident of Bala Town Council,and two others identified as Okello and Walter,who are reportedly residents of Lira City.</p><p>Police have opened investigations to establish the ownership of the livestock,how the animals were obtained and whether the suspects are connected to other livestock theft cases in the region.</p><p>The incident has raised concerns over the growing tension surrounding livestock theft in communities,with authorities urging residents to report suspected criminal activity to police instead of taking the law into their own hands.</p><p>Police are also expected to establish the circumstances under which the vehicle was set ablaze and whether any further action will be taken against those involved.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/7bb4a5322116c778.jpg', 'Scrap of the burned Vehicle', 2, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 0, 0, '2026-08-13 19:47:15', '2026-08-13 19:47:15', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(38, 'Residents Burnt Suspected Livestock Theft Vehicle to Ashes in Kwania,Four Arrested.', 'residents-burnt-suspected-livestock-theft-vehicle-to-ashes-in-kwania-four-arrested-2', 'By Hillary Opio Omara KWANIA DISTRICT: Residents of Bung in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Kwania District,reportedly set fire to a Toyota Noah vehicle suspect…', '<p><strong>By Hillary Opio Omara </strong></p><p><strong>KWANIA DISTRICT: </strong>Residents of Bung in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Kwania District,reportedly set fire to a Toyota Noah vehicle suspected of being used to transport stolen livestock,as police arrested four people in connection with the alleged theft.</p><p>The incident occurred today Thursday,August 13,2026,after residents reportedly became suspicious of the vehicle and raised an alarm over livestock allegedly loaded inside it.</p><p>Moses Amwata,the Bung LC1 Chairperson, told Radio Q FM that residents noticed the Toyota Noah parked in the area and decided to investigate.</p><p>According to Amwata,residents discovered livestock inside the vehicle that they suspected had been stolen.</p><p>The situation reportedly escalated,with angry residents setting the vehicle ablaze and reducing it to ashes.</p><p>Lucy Achato,a resident and livestock owner, said the alleged theft angered residents and prompted them to intervene after becoming suspicious about the animals and the vehicle.</p><p>Dorcus Wangari,the Aduku Town Council Councilor said she received a report from the Gender and Integrated Security Office (GISO) and that she visited the scene to assess the situation.</p><p>Wangari urged residents to avoid transporting livestock at night without proper documentation.</p><p>She said livestock buyers should have documents proving ownership and showing where the animals were legally purchased.</p><p>“People should not move livestock at night without documents showing that they legally bought the animals,” Wangari said.</p><p>Kwania District Police Commander SP Kadoogo Paul confirmed that police received a report on August 13,2026, concerning a Toyota Noah registration number UAP 736K,which was allegedly being used to transport suspected stolen livestock.</p><p>He said police intervened and arrested the driver together with three other people who were inside the vehicle.</p><p>Geoffrey Okello,the GISO of Aduku Town Council,said preliminary information indicates that some of the livestock allegedly involved in the incident originated from Bala in Kole District and Akalo,among other areas.</p><p>The suspects arrested include Emmanuel Opio,a resident of Adyeda Trading Centre in Teduka Ward,Aduku Town Council,Opio Ashan,also known as Murefo,a resident of Bala Town Council,and two others identified as Okello and Walter,who are reportedly residents of Lira City.</p><p>Police have opened investigations to establish the ownership of the livestock,how the animals were obtained and whether the suspects are connected to other livestock theft cases in the region.</p><p>The incident has raised concerns over the growing tension surrounding livestock theft in communities,with authorities urging residents to report suspected criminal activity to police instead of taking the law into their own hands.</p><p>Police are also expected to establish the circumstances under which the vehicle was set ablaze and whether any further action will be taken against those involved</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/5085853a4c9ec701.jpg', 'Burned car ( scrap)', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 0, 283, '2026-08-13 20:07:36', '2026-09-03 03:14:33', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(39, 'Boda-Boda Riders in Alebtong Demand Shs217m Election Mobilisation Money.', 'boda-boda-riders-in-alebtong-demand-shs217m-election-mobilisation-money', 'By Hillary Opio Omara ALEBTONG DISTRICT - Boda-Boda riders in Alebtong District have accused the NRM leadership in the district of withholding Shs217 million a…', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara </p><p>ALEBTONG DISTRICT - Boda-Boda riders in Alebtong District have accused the NRM leadership in the district of withholding Shs217 million allegedly sent to support about 3,000 bodaboda operators who helped mobilise voters during the January 2026 general elections.</p><p>The riders claim the money was sent as compensation for their activities during the election period,but they say they have never received it.</p><p>Speaking to OromaTv in the North Kyoga Regional Office in Lira City on Thursday 13,2026,Alebtong District Boda-Boda Chairperson Richard Ewany-Ewany said the riders are demanding accountability for the funds.</p><p>Ewany-Ewany said the money was reportedly meant for approximately 3,000 bodaboda riders who participated in activities aimed at mobilising voters during the elections.</p><p>He said the riders want an explanation from Alebtong District NRM Chairperson Robert Ocen Abia,whom they accuse of holding the money.</p><p>The bodaboda leaders said they are prepared to listen to Ocen\'s explanation but want transparency on how the funds were received and used.</p><p>Several riders,including Dickens Okello and Robert Opio,expressed frustration,saying they worked hard during the election period but have allegedly not benefited from the money reportedly sent for them.</p><p>They said receiving the funds would help them address various challenges affecting their families and livelihoods.</p><p>In response,Alebtong District NRM Chairperson Robert Ocen Abia denied that the money was intended to pay individual bodaboda riders.</p><p>Ocen told Radio Q FM that the funds were meant for voter mobilisation and election-related activities,including supporting activities to encourage people to turn up and vote,rather than direct payments to individual bodaboda operators.</p><p>He further suggested that the complaints could be linked to individuals attempting to create confusion over the purpose and management of the funds.</p><p>The bodaboda riders,however,maintain that the money was intended to support them and are demanding a clear account of how it was handled.</p><p>The riders are now calling for transparency and accountability over the alleged Shs217 million,saying they want to know who received the money,how it was spent and why they were not paid.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/c6f6dee66dadc9ba.jpg', 'Alebtong District Boda-Boda Chairperson Richard Ewany-Ewany says riders want accountability for Shs217 million allegedly sent for election mobilisation.', 3, 1, NULL, 'Boda- boda riders in Alebtong District are demanding Shs217 million allegedly sent by NRM to compensate 3,000 operators who mobilised voters during the January 2026 elections.', 'published', 0, 70, '2026-08-14 13:28:04', '2026-09-02 15:39:33', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(40, 'The beacon welcomes over  1000  new Students , set focus  on skills and responsible leadership', 'the-beacon-welcomes-over-1000-new-students-set-focus-on-skills-and-responsible-leadership', 'By Isaac Erick Odongo LIRA CITY — Lira University has welcomed more than 1000 newly admitted students for the 2026/2027 academic year, with university leadersh…', '<p>By Isaac Erick Odongo </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY —</strong> Lira University has welcomed more than 1000 newly admitted students for the 2026/2027 academic year, with university leadership urging them to acquire practical skills and become responsible citizens capable of contributing to the development of Uganda and the wider Lango sub-region.</p><p>Speaking during activities to welcome the new students, Lira University Vice Chancellor, Prof. Jaspher Watson Ogwal Okeng, said the institution is committed to producing graduates who can stand on their own and contribute meaningfully to national development.</p><p>He encouraged the students to go beyond acquiring academic knowledge and focus on developing practical skills that can be applied in the workplace and other areas of society.</p><p>Ogwal Okeng also commended President Yoweri Kaguta Museveni for supporting the growth of the university and promoting infrastructure development, saying the investments have contributed to raising the institution\'s profile and expanding access to higher education in the region.</p><p>Lira City Resident City Commissioner Emmy Lawrence Egole challenged the newly admitted students to embrace responsible leadership and help identify challenges affecting their communities.</p><p>Egole urged the students to work with university authorities and fellow students to find practical solutions to challenges that may affect their welfare and academic progress.</p><p>He also encouraged students to make proper use of the available sports and other university facilities, saying such activities can help promote talent, discipline and teamwork while contributing to the development of Lira University and the Lango sub-region.</p><p>Associate Professor Judith Abal, who is serving as Acting Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic Affairs, said the university is prepared to support the new students throughout their academic journey.</p><p>Abal encouraged students facing academic or other challenges to seek guidance from her office and other relevant university authorities instead of keeping their problems to themselves.</p><p>She urged the students to take advantage of the available support systems to ensure a smooth academic experience at Lira University.</p><p>Lira University Guild President Benedict Arac welcomed the new students and urged them to respect university rules and regulations.</p><p>Arac called on students to maintain discipline, respect one another and make responsible decisions throughout their time at the university.</p><p>Lira University admitted 3,320 new students for the 2025/2026 academic year, compared with 2,345 students admitted in the previous academic year, reflecting continued growth in student enrolment at the institution.</p><p>The university leadership says the growing enrolment presents an opportunity to expand access to higher education while equipping young people with the knowledge, skills and values needed to contribute to Uganda\'s development.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/a0b2451c2db58d9e.jpg', 'Newly admitted students during the 2026/2027 orientation at Lira University', 10, 1, NULL, 'Lira University has admitted over 1,000 new students for the 2026/2027 academic year. VC Prof. Ogwal Okeng urged them to acquire practical skills and become responsible citizens.', 'published', 1, 43, '2026-08-14 14:25:09', '2026-08-31 01:57:42', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(41, 'Minister Engola Delivers Promised Vehicle to Abunga Parish Reverend', 'minister-engola-delivers-promised-vehicle-to-abunga-parish-reverend', 'Minister Sam Engola has fulfilled a pledge to donate a new Subaru to Reverend Nelson Peter Okullo of Abunga Parish to support pastoral duties.', '<h2>Minister Fulfills Pledge to Abunga Parish</h2><p>Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, Sam Engola, has delivered on a promise to provide a vehicle for the Reverend of Abunga Parish. The donation aims to enhance pastoral work, evangelism, and community outreach efforts within the parish.</p><h3>Vehicle Handover Ceremony</h3><p>A brand-new Subaru, registered as UA 316 FC, was officially handed over to Reverend Nelson Peter Okullo, the Catechist of Abunga Parish Church of Uganda, during a ceremony at St. Lira Hotel. Benson Emor, representing Minister Engola, stated that the minister had pledged the vehicle in March 2026 to facilitate the Reverend\'s movements for pastoral duties.</p><h3>Strengthening Church Mission and Community Ties</h3><p>The vehicle is intended to bolster the Church\'s mission of spreading the gospel, conducting pastoral visits, and engaging with local communities. Emor also called for closer collaboration between religious and civic leaders to address social issues such as violence, crime, and domestic abuse affecting families.</p><h3>Call for Support to Livelihood Initiatives</h3><p>Additionally, Emor encouraged church leaders to champion government initiatives focused on improving household livelihoods and promoting wealth creation programs among the populace.</p><h3>Reverend Okullo Expresses Gratitude</h3><p>Reverend Okullo expressed his sincere thanks to Minister Engola for fulfilling his pledge. He highlighted that the new vehicle would significantly ease his ability to deliver pastoral services to communities, particularly in areas where transportation remains a challenge. Reverend Okullo also offered prayers for the Minister and his family, encouraging continued support for communities as a divine calling. </p><h3>Commitment to Responsible Use</h3><p>Reverend Okullo pledged to utilize the vehicle responsibly, committing to adhere to road safety regulations and show respect to fellow road users.</p><h3>Archdeacon Welcomes Donation</h3><p>The Archdeacon of Lira Archdeaconry, Reverend Jacob Acon, welcomed the donation, noting its importance in facilitating regular pastoral visits to Christians across the parish. Citing Proverbs 19:17, Reverend Acon thanked Minister Engola and urged Reverend Okullo to leverage the vehicle to expand pastoral outreach and ensure the wider dissemination of God\'s message.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/069bc83a8a31f1b4.webp', NULL, 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 27, '2026-08-15 06:16:00', '2026-09-02 18:12:25', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(42, 'UPC Baraza on Apire election violence Postponed by security.', 'upc-baraza-on-apire-election-violence-postponed-by-security', 'By Hillary Opio Omara KWANIA DISTRICT - Security authorities in Kwania District have postponed a planned Uganda People’s Congress (UPC) Baraza aimed at address…', '<p><strong>By Hillary Opio Omara </strong></p><p>KWANIA DISTRICT - Security authorities in Kwania District have postponed a planned Uganda People’s Congress (UPC) Baraza aimed at addressing tensions arising from violence during the recent LC2 election in Apire Parish,Aduku Sub-county.</p><p>The decision follows disagreements among security officials and leaders of the UPC and National Resistance Movement (NRM) over how the post-election tensions should be handled.</p><p>The violence,which occurred on Monday at Acut Trading Centre and Bung in Apire Parish,reportedly left more than five people injured,including police officers and civilians.A police vehicle was also reportedly vandalized during the confrontation.</p><p>According to police reports,Kwania District Police Commander (DPC) SP Kadoogo Paul received a telephone report about clashes between supporters of the UPC and NRM during the election of the Apire Parish LC2 chairperson.</p><p>The DPC,accompanied by the police driver, Deputy Resident District Commissioner (RDC) Aturu Abraham,the Deputy District Internal Security Officer,the Kwania District Electoral Commission Returning Officer and other police officers,rushed to the area to restore order.</p><p>However,the situation reportedly escalated, resulting in injuries to some police officers and residents and damage to the police vehicle.</p><p>Speaking to journalists at Kwania Resort Hotel today Saturday August 15,2026,Emmanuel Opio Okello,the NRM Publicity Secretary for Kwania District,said the party had received information from Kwania District Woman MP Kenney Auma Lapat about a planned meeting involving NRM leaders,the offices of the DPC and RDC, and the UPDF 5th Division Commander.</p><p>Opio Okello questioned the decision to involve NRM leaders and their supporters in the proposed meeting,arguing that accusations made by UPC supporters before the DPC and Deputy RDC should first have been addressed through the appropriate leadership structures.</p><p>NRM Kwania District Chairman Nelson Sadam Abili accused MP Kenney Auma of repeatedly inciting residents during election periods,claiming that similar incidents occurred during the presidential,LC5 and most recently the LC2 elections.</p><p>However,Kwania Assistant RDC Ceaser Obada said the Baraza was cancelled after consultations with the RDC and police as investigations into the Apire Parish violence continue.</p><p>Obada said the meeting could not proceed while six suspects allegedly linked to the violence remained in police custody.</p><p><strong>On Blue coat is ARDC Kwania district Ceaser Obada</strong> </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/0dc96b4034ede9e1.jpg\"></p><p>MP Kenney Auma defended her decision to convene the meeting,saying her objective was to restore peace and bring together leaders who had disagreed following the election violence.</p><p>Auma said about six UPC supporters had been arrested and detained at Kwania Central Police Station in connection with the incident.</p><p>Although the Baraza has been postponed, Auma said she intends to hold a separate meeting with residents of Apire to hear their concerns and engage local leaders on possible ways of resolving the tensions.</p><p>North Kyoga Regional Police spokesperson SP Patrick Jimmy Okema said police had not received an official report about the planned Baraza but confirmed that investigations into the Apire Parish violence were ongoing.</p><p>SP Okema said the investigations are being conducted under SD:REF:40/10/08/2026, SD:REF:43/10/08/2026 and GEF:13/2026.</p><p>He said police had recorded statements from witnesses and arrested four people suspected of participating in the violence.</p><p>According to Okema,the case files have since been sanctioned by the Resident State Attorney (RSA) in Apac District,paving the way for further legal action against the suspects.</p><p>The postponement comes amid heightened political tensions in Apire Parish,with security authorities maintaining that investigations must be allowed to proceed before any reconciliation meeting involving the parties can take place.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/65ee926216db66bb.jpg', 'Woman MP Kwania district Hon Auma Kenny Lapat set for the Baraza before it was  stopped by security', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 76, '2026-08-15 14:55:56', '2026-09-03 05:56:13', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(43, 'PM Nabbanja Donates Shs10 Million to Loro Catholic Parish in Oyam', 'pm-nabbanja-donates-shs10-million-to-loro-catholic-parish-in-oyam', 'Prime Minister Robinah Nabbanja has donated Shs10 million to St. Mary’s Catholic Parish in Loro, Oyam District for chairs and church construction. The donation was made during Assumption Day celebrations.', '<p>By Issac Erick Odongo </p><p><strong>LORO, OYAM DISTRICT —</strong> Prime Minister Robinah Nabbanja has donated Shs10 million towards the purchase of chairs and development of St. Mary’s Catholic Parish in Loro, Oyam District.</p><p>Nabbanja through the Oyam district woman MP Hon Santa Alum Ogwang made the contribution during the opening of the church and celebrations at the parish, where she commended the Catholic Church for its continued contribution to social and economic development in communities.</p><p>She said the Church has played an important role in supporting government programmes and mobilising communities, particularly through initiatives such as the Parish Development Model (PDM), Emyooga and other government interventions aimed at improving household incomes and livelihoods.</p><p><strong>Woman MP for Oyam District Santa Alum Ogwang Handed over the money to the Church leaders </strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/a702bfcf7c708846.jpg\"></p><p>According to Nabbanja, the contribution would be used to purchase chairs and other construction materials required to advance work on the church building .</p><p>Oyam District Member of Parliament Santa Alum Ogwang welcomed Nabbanja\'s contribution and commended Christians of Loro Catholic Parish for their commitment to the construction project.</p><p>Alum particularly recognised the work of the parish priest, Fr. Peter Panya, and the Christian community, saying their determination and collective effort had enabled the construction of the church to make significant progress.</p><p>Alum also thanked Members of Parliament from Lango and other parts of Uganda for contributing financially and supporting the construction project.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c92ec018a2ca7298.jpg\"></p><p>The legislator pledged to continue mobilising additional support for development initiatives in Lango, saying leaders have a responsibility to work together to attract resources and promote projects that benefit communities.</p><p>Bishop Emeritus Joseph Franzelli congratulated the Christians of Loro Parish for their commitment, sacrifice and perseverance in seeing the church construction project through.</p><p>He encouraged the faithful to maintain their unity and continue supporting the project until all outstanding works are completed.</p><p>Meanwhile Bishop Santus Lino Wanok the ordinary of Lira diocese, who led the prayers during the celebrations, called on church leaders, political leaders and Christians to continue working together for the development of the Church and the wider community.</p><p>Wanok emphasised the importance of unity and cooperation among leaders and faithful, urging them to put aside differences and work collectively.</p><p>The event at Loro Catholic Parish also coincided with the Catholic Church\'s annual celebration of the Solemnity of the Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary, observed every year on August 15.</p><p>The feast commemorates the Catholic belief that the Virgin Mary was taken body and soul into heavenly glory at the end of her earthly life.</p><p>The celebration brought together Catholic faithful, religious leaders, political leaders and other members of the community for prayers, thanksgiving and fellowship.</p><p>The occasion also provided an opportunity for the faithful to renew their commitment to the development of the parish and mobilise additional support for the purchase  of the church.</p><p>The Loro project is part of the wider efforts by Catholic communities in the region to establish and improve places of worship and related facilities to serve growing congregations.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/88583be104f7c297.jpg', 'St Mary\'s Catholic Parish in Loro Oyam district', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 60, '2026-08-15 20:32:19', '2026-09-02 18:37:40', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(44, 'Lango Diocese Donates Shs 8.5 Million to Support Thanksgiving Prayer for LRA Returnees', 'lango-diocese-donates-shs-8-5-million-to-support-thanksgiving-prayer-for-lra-returnees', 'The Diocese of Lango has donated *Shs 8.5 million  to support a thanksgiving prayer service for former LRA captives and returnees scheduled for September 12, 2026 at Boroboro Cathedral, Lira City.', '<p>By Isaac Erick Odongo </p><p><strong>LIRA LANGO- </strong>The Diocese of Lango has committed Shs 8.5 million towards preparations for a major thanksgiving prayer service for former LRA captives and returnees, as religious leaders and survivors prepare to gather in Lira next month.</p><p>The funds will support preparations for the thanksgiving service organized by the Lango Captives and Returnees Association, which brings together people who were abducted and affected by the Lord’s Resistance Army (LRA) insurgency.</p><p>The thanksgiving service is intended to give survivors and their families an opportunity to thank God for their survival, return and restoration after years of captivity and displacement.</p><p>The Diocese’s financial support follows consultations between the Lango Captives and Returnees Association and religious leaders on how to organize the event and meet the logistical costs involved.</p><p>Speaking to OromaTv on August 14, 2026, shortly after a meeting at Lira Hotel, Abel Ogeny, the association’s coordinator and representative for northern Uganda, said the Diocese of Lango had agreed to provide Shs 8.5 million to help cover the costs of organizing the prayer service.</p><p>Ogeny said the financial support is expected to ease some of the burden on the organizers, who have been mobilizing resources to prepare for the event.</p><p><strong><em>Abel Ogeny in a standing meeting with some leaders  some members as they prepare for the upcoming event ( Thanksgiving prayer)</em></strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/374cae332c4079c0.jpg\"></p><p>He said the association’s leadership is also continuing to look for additional support to meet other expenses ahead of the thanksgiving service.</p><p>Ogeny said the contribution comes at a time when the association is preparing to bring together a large number of former captives, returnees, religious leaders, families and other community members for the special prayers.</p><p>He added that the event is expected to provide an important platform for survivors to reflect on their experiences, give thanks for their return and pray for continued peace and healing in communities that were affected by the LRA conflict.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/5b33a7ede6dffb95.jpg\"></p><p>Rev. Tonny Joshua Olet, who spoke on behalf of the Lango religious leaders, said the Diocese considered the difficult experiences of people who were abducted and forced into captivity during the insurgency before agreeing to support the initiative.</p><p>Olet said the thanksgiving should remain centred on prayer and giving thanks to God for protecting the survivors and enabling them to return to their communities.</p><p>He appealed to members of the public, particularly people from the affected communities, to support and participate in the event.</p><p>Some of the returnees who spoke to our reporter also expressed optimism that the prayers would provide an opportunity for former captives and their families to seek God\'s continued guidance, healing and blessings.</p><p>They said the event could also strengthen solidarity among communities that experienced the effects of the LRA insurgency and provide an opportunity to remember the difficult past while looking forward to a more peaceful future.</p><p>The thanksgiving prayer service is scheduled for September 12, 2026, at Boroboro Cathedral in Lira City.</p><p>Organizers expect the event to attract more than 1,000 people from the Lango and Acholi sub-regions, including former captives, returnees, their relatives, religious leaders and other members of the public.</p><p>Hon. Sam Engola, Minister of State for Disaster Preparedness, Relief and Refugees, is also expected to attend the event as the guest of honour.</p><p>With the Diocese of Lango’s Shs 8.5 million contribution now committed, organizers say they will continue mobilizing additional resources to complete preparations and ensure that the thanksgiving service is successfully held.</p><p>For the former captives and returnees, the event is expected to serve not only as a religious gathering, but also as a moment to reflect on their journey from captivity to freedom and to give thanks for the opportunity to rebuild their lives and communities.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/2580468b2704fe73.jpg', 'Some members of the LRA affected persons attended the Meeting ahead of the Thanksgiving prayer', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 58, '2026-08-15 22:14:11', '2026-08-31 12:30:41', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(45, 'UPDF Commences Recruitment in Greater Bushenyi as Man Arrested Over Alleged Bribe Attempt', 'updf-commences-recruitment-in-greater-bushenyi-as-man-arrested-over-alleged-bribe-attempt', 'The Uganda People’s Defence Forces  UPDF has commenced recruitment in Greater Bushenyi, and Mitooma districts .', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p><strong>BUSHENYI / MASINDI | August 16, 2026</strong></p><p>The Uganda People’s Defence Forces UPDF has commenced recruitment in Greater Bushenyi, and Mitooma districts .</p><p>The UPDF General Recruitment Exercise 2026 physical selection phase officially commenced nationwide on August 10, 2026, and runs through August 22, 2026.</p><p>According to Maj. Edward Birungi, following a Post on UPDF Whatsapp group on Sunday, 16th August, the recruitment team spokesperson, candidates are undergoing physical and medical screening, followed by document verification. Eligible youth who meet the set requirements are expected to proceed to the next stages of the exercise.</p><p>The UPDF recruitment in Greater Bushenyi is part of the army’s ongoing nationwide drive to enlist new soldiers.</p><p>In a related development, the UPDF recruitment team in Masindi District arrested a man on Tuesday over an alleged attempt to bribe his way into the army.</p><p>Emmanuel Kyakabaale Tayebwa, a resident of Kimengo Sub-county, was arrested at the Masindi District Headquarters where the recruitment exercise was ongoing.</p><p>According to the recruitment team, Kyakabaale was initially disqualified after failing to produce a valid Uganda Certificate of Education - UCE. He had instead presented a Primary Seven certificate and a Senior Four pass slip.</p><p>Officials say the suspect allegedly attempted to offer Shs 20,000 to recruitment officers in a bid to be considered despite not meeting the academic requirements.</p><p>He is currently in police custody as investigations continue.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/54abec155628fb82.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Emmanuel Kyakabaale Taayebwa resident o kimengo sub county was arrested on Tuesday Photo by URN</em></strong></p><p>Maj. Birungi warned that the UPDF has a zero-tolerance policy on bribery and forgery during recruitment and urged applicants to follow the laid-down procedures.</p><p>“Anyone found attempting to bribe or forge documents will be arrested and prosecuted,” Birungi said.</p><p><strong>Recruitment Requirements</strong></p><p>The UPDF recruitment exercise requires applicants to present original academic documents, national ID, birth certificate, and letters of recommendation from LC1 and RDC. Candidates must also pass physical fitness and medical tests.</p><p>The army says the recruitment drive aims to ensure transparency, discipline and that only qualified Ugandan join the forces.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/79629dd49e71f520.jpg', 'Bushenyi District :Applicants under go physical and medical screening followed by by Document verification', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 91, '2026-08-16 08:04:50', '2026-08-31 10:32:13', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(46, 'Leaders Gather at Gracious Palace Hotel for Gracious Group Principal\'s Dinner', 'leaders-gather-at-gracious-palace-hotel-for-gracious-group-principal-s-dinner', 'The Gracious Group of Companies held its annual Principals’ Dinner on Sunday, August 16, 2026 at Gracious Palace Hotel Caleb Square', '<p>BY Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY -The</strong> Gracious Group of Companies on Sunday hosted its annual Principals’ Dinner at Gracious Palace Hotel - Caleb Square, bringing together leaders from SAGRASS Schools, Primary Schools, Gracious Palace Hotel (GPH), and House of Buttons to share experiences, reflect on the year, and lay out plans for the future.</p><p>This year’s dinner marks a transformation from the Directors’ Dinner to a full Gracious Group of Companies gathering, organized under the stewardship of Hon :Elem Leo, MP Moroto County, Alebtong District, who also serves as Principal of St. Gracious Schools Day &amp; Boarding and St. Gracious Nursery and Primary.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/06fa00a5964ed57b.jpg\"></p><p>Welcoming guests, Saul George William, General Manager of Gracious Palace Hotel Ltd, reflected on 15 years of service.  </p><p>He attributed the hotel’s growth to teamwork, commitment, and the support of member companies under the Gracious Group umbrella.</p><p><strong><em>General Manager Gracious Palace Hotel </em></strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/906de1ec7839283f.jpg\"></p><p>CEO of Gracious Group of Companies, Dr Patrick Olet,   informed principals that the group has grown into a big company with expanding influence.</p><p>He thanked Hon. Elem Leo for organizing “such a big dinner,” noting he has known him for almost 20 years and described him as a person of humility through whom “God has come to stand tall and make sure the company grows.”</p><p>Olet in the middle of  his communication,urged members to remain committed to their calling, </p><p>“The expectation is to have courage and build a name or brand. </p><p>Whether you are a teacher or a receptionist all the staff, You are the face of the business and the ambassador,” he said.</p><p><strong><em>CEO Gracious Companies Group Dr Patrick Olet  addresses the  Principals who came to  Gracious Palace Hotel for the Dinner </em></strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c25f23773fd46ab2.jpg\"></p><p>“As Gracious Group we want to see others grow together. Next year our focus will be on individual growth,” he added.</p><p>Meanwhile , Hon. Elem Leo thanked the family of Patrick Olet , whom he credited for his personal and professional success.</p><p>He testified that Dr. Patrick Olet was the first person he consulted before joining politics in the 2026  Elections that  challenges the the Negative attitude by his Parents about politics </p><p>Speaking on his first four ( 4)months in the 12th Parliament and his debut,  Hon. Elem Leo said:  My being there will not only help the people of Moroto.” but for the Nation Uganda and it\'s Citizens </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/da2ffc2bd8476f2b.jpg\"></p><p>He however stressed that  teaching remains his best calling because being in Parliament can Only have impacts if the policies which the legislators always make are  respected through implementations. \"In other words no implementations No Impacts\' </p><p>“The teaching I did has changed the lives of people. One can be in Parliament for money, \"but not to create   impacts in the lives of citizens\'\', said Elem Leo.</p><p>In business, he hailed  Gracious Group as “the best company in the country”</p><p> and ranked Gracious Palace Hotel the Best with all the facilities , noting that competitors “don’t have Spa and Gym floor such as Weight Machines and running tracks Sauna or Steam Rooms locker rooms Among others, </p><p><strong><em>The team inspects the Spa and Gym Floor  such as weight machines and running tracks,  Sauna or steam </em></strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/6bdfcbacb671cc1f.jpg\"></p><p>The dinner closed with a renewed call for unity, service, and brand building across all Gracious Group entities.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/57fc48e06eca9d19.jpg', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 20, '2026-08-17 13:13:39', '2026-08-31 01:14:33', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(47, 'Authorities in Lira City  Demands Answers from Land Officials Over Missing from Office', 'authorities-in-lira-city-demands-answers-from-land-officials-over-missing-from-office', 'BY Hillary Opio Omara LIRA CITY - Lira City East Division authorities have given land officials one day to explain why they were absent from their offices,afte…', '<p>BY Hillary Opio Omara </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY</strong> - Lira City East Division authorities have given land officials one day to explain why they were absent from their offices,after an inspection found several government staff away from their duty stations.</p><p>The directive was issued on Monday,August 17,2026,after the Lira City East Division Mayor,Denis Peter Odongo Odul,together with the Resident City Commissioner and other officials,inspected land-related offices in Lira City.</p><p>During the inspection,the officials reportedly found some government employees who were expected to provide land services absent from their offices,leaving members of the public seeking services unattended.</p><p>Odongo Odul said the division had been receiving complaints about poor service delivery at the land offices for some time, including concerns over delays in accessing land documents and other services.</p><p>He said the inspection team found only one person at the reception,while some other individuals identified as interns were also present.</p><p>According to Odongo Odul,the absence of responsible officers raises concerns about the delivery of essential land services to residents.</p><p>He said the affected officials have been given one day to explain what prevented them from being at their duty stations.</p><p>The mayor warned that failure to provide a satisfactory explanation could result in further action against the concerned officials.</p><p>He also said starting Tuesday,August 18, 2026,the division would closely monitor attendance and service delivery at the offices to ensure that government employees remain available to serve the public.</p><p>Odongo Odul further noted that difficulties in obtaining land documents,particularly land titles,have become a growing concern among residents and should not be worsened by the absence of responsible officers.</p><p>Meanwhile, Deputy Resident City Commissioner Steven Odongo said government employs public servants to deliver services to citizens and urged them to respect their official responsibilities.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/0e79339056b45c58.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Deputy RCC Steven Odongo </em></strong></p><p>He criticized officials who fail to remain at their duty stations while members of the public are waiting for services.</p><p>Odongo said government workers should use their positions to serve the public rather than prioritize personal financial interests at the expense of service delivery.</p><p>He warned that officials found responsible for negligence or poor service delivery would face accountability measures.</p><p>\"We shall write the letter to Ministry of Land,Housing and Urban Development to address this challenge if these officials can\'t explain anything to them\"Steven Odongo said.</p><p>Attempts by Radio OromaTv to reach the officer in charge of the Lira  land office for a comment were unsuccessful,as he was reportedly in Kampala at the time.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/4ee163d7ac54c8c1.jpg', 'Mayor Lira city East Denis Peter Odongo Odul', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 38, '2026-08-17 22:46:47', '2026-08-31 09:02:46', 0, 1, 'inter');
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `excerpt`, `content`, `featured_image`, `featured_image_caption`, `category_id`, `author_id`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `status`, `is_featured`, `views`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_breaking`, `reading_time`, `body_font`) VALUES
(48, 'UPDF Recruitment:Otuke Man Arrested Over Alleged Defilement Case.', 'updf-recruitment-otuke-man-arrested-over-alleged-defilement-case', 'The suspect,identified as Michael Ojok,a resident of Corner Adwari in Otuke District, was arrested on Monday,August 17,2026, while appearing for the UPDF recruitment exercise at Mayor Gardens in Lira City.', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara </p><p>OTUKE/ ALEBTONG - A Man  from Otuke District has been arrested during the ongoing Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) recruitment exercise after being accused of defiling a teenage girl in Adwari Sub-county.</p><p>The suspect,identified as Michael Ojok,a resident of Corner Adwari in Otuke District, was arrested on Monday,August 17,2026, while appearing for the UPDF recruitment exercise at Mayor Gardens in Lira City.</p><p>Ojok had reportedly travelled to Lira to participate in the recruitment exercise, which on Monday entered its second day for applicants from Otuke and Alebtong districts.</p><p>According to Isaac Opio Opeo,the Assistant Resident District Commissioner (ARDC) of Otuke,a report was filed at Otuke Central Police Station on June 27,2026,accusing Ojok of defiling a minor.</p><p>Opio Opeo said police had been searching for the suspect before his arrest during the UPDF recruitment exercise.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/4261d41a9dc4e881.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>ARDC Otuke Issac Opio Opeo witness and confirmed the arrest of the suspect </em></strong></p><p>He explained that after Ojok was identified among the applicants at the recruitment centre,he contacted the Otuke District Police Commander (DPC),who confirmed that the suspect was wanted in connection with the case.</p><p>The ARDC subsequently directed police officers to arrest Ojok and return him to Otuke Central Police Station,where he is expected to face further investigation.</p><p>Meanwhile,Lameck Ongom,the Assistant RDC of Alebtong District,said two people were arrested during the recruitment exercise that took place in Lira Mayor Garden on suspicion of forgery.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c66ef1916d8a82b4.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>ARDC Alebtong district Lameck Ongom  speaks to the Press on recruitment</em></strong> </p><p>The suspects reportedly included one female and one male from Alebtong district,whom police prevented from proceeding with the recruitment after allegedly detecting irregularities in their documents.</p><p>Speaking on the arrests,Major Bilal Katamba, the UPDF spokesperson for the 4th Division Infantry covering the Acholi Sub-region and West Nile,confirmed that the recruitment exercise was progressing well.</p><p>Maj.Katamba said the exercise began on August 10,2026,across the Acholi and Lango sub-regions.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/7da5b792351a4f1c.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Maj.Bilal Katamba </em></strong></p><p>He urged applicants to maintain good conduct and warned that recruitment into the UPDF requires individuals to have a good reputation and clean records within their communities.</p><p>According to the recruitment figures,76 applicants have so far been recruited from Alebtong District,while 76 have been recruited from Otuke District.</p><p>The recruitment team is scheduled to continue the exercise in Dokolo and Amolatar districts on Tuesday,August 18, 2026.</p><p>Authorities have continued to encourage eligible young people to follow the official recruitment procedures and provide genuine documents during the exercise.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/f04bc53ef54fefd0.jpg', NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 'man from Otuke District has been arrested during the ongoing Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) recruitment exercise after being accused of defiling a teenage girl in Adwari Sub-county.\r\n\r\nThe suspect,identified as Michael Ojok,a resident of Corner Adwari in Otuke District, was arrested on Monday,August 17,2026, while appearing for the UPDF recruitment exercise at Mayor Gardens in Lira City.\r\n\r\nOjok had reportedly travelled to Lira to participate in the recruitment exercise, which on Monday e', 'published', 1, 27, '2026-08-18 09:50:43', '2026-09-01 21:22:04', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(49, 'Four Alito Town Council LC2 Chairpersons Reported Over Alleged Restocking Funds Fraud', 'four-alito-town-council-lc2-chairpersons-reported-over-alleged-restocking-funds-fraud', 'The officials are accused of allegedly using the names and identities of verified beneficiaries to withdraw compensation money without their knowledge or consent.', '<p>By  Isaac Erick Odongo </p><p>KOLE — Four LC2 Chairpersons from Alito Town Council in Kole District are set to record statements with police over allegations of irregularities in the distribution of government restocking compensation funds.</p><p>The officials are accused of allegedly using the names and identities of verified beneficiaries to withdraw compensation money without their knowledge or consent.</p><p>The allegations emerged during a meeting at Alito Town Council headquarters on Monday, August 17, where beneficiaries who had complained about the payments confronted officials over what they described as irregularities in the disbursement process.</p><p><em>Photo by Isaac Erick Odongo </em></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/fd5f9de743e0bafc.jpg\"></p><p>Alito Town Council Mayor Benedict Obote told our reporter that complaints had been received from all four wards, involving about 11 people who reportedly received compensation funds.</p><p>According to Obote, nine of those who received the money were allegedly government employees, while three others were reportedly individuals from neighbouring districts.</p><p>In Tekidi Ward, Town Agent Dorcus Ekit and Veterinary Officer Emmanuel Enyabu are accused of collecting money using the names of Joshua Ogwang and Nancy Akello, despite the two beneficiaries reportedly not being present to receive the funds.</p><p>In Owani-Adilo Ward, Town Clerk Rebecca Abonyo allegedly collected money in the name of Timothy Odongo, while Town Agent Okello Sam is accused of using the name of Wilson Omongo.</p><p>Obote also cited the case of Sarah Apio, who allegedly consented to someone collecting money in the name of Grace Obote. Grace reportedly received only Shs250,000 out of the Shs5 million compensation due to her, leaving Shs4.75 million unpaid.</p><p>In Akor Ward, CDO Mistika Atiti allegedly used the name of Immaculate Anena to collect funds, while Town Agent Patrick Otim is accused of collecting money in the name of Awino Jenet.</p><p>In Bua-Tyeno Ward, Town Agent George Okello allegedly used the name of Auma Anna, while Town Clerk Rebecca Abonyo is accused of collecting money in the name of Akello Sophia.</p><p>The alleged beneficiaries, however, reportedly denied authorising the officials to collect the funds on their behalf.</p><p>Obote described the allegations as serious and said they could point to wider failures in the management of the compensation programme.</p><p>He also questioned the alleged involvement of some former local leaders, including former Alito Town Council LC3 chairperson Moses Ojok, in payments that were reportedly collected using names that did not correspond with the rightful beneficiaries.</p><p>Obote directed Alito Town Council staff to ensure that government funds meant for restocking and other compensation programmes reach the rightful beneficiaries.</p><p>He said local leaders have a responsibility to safeguard public funds and ensure that the compensation programme achieves its intended purpose.</p><p>Alito Town Council councillor Tamali Auma, who represents women at the district, urged government officials and local leaders to strictly follow guidelines governing the compensation programme.</p><p>Tamali also called for beneficiaries who have lodged complaints to be assisted in recovering any money that may have been wrongly taken from them.</p><p>Another councillor, Charles Okello, called on government officials to ensure that compensation funds withheld from beneficiaries are recovered and paid to the rightful recipients.</p><p>Okello, who represents Bua-Tyeno Ward at LC2 level, said local leaders had already raised concerns with government officials but had been reluctant to pursue the matter aggressively over fears that some could lose their jobs.</p><p>Following Monday\'s meeting, the nine officials implicated in the complaints are expected to report to Kole Central Police Station within five days to respond to the allegations.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/9ed0a7e2361558f6.jpg\"></p><p>The allegations come amid the government\'s restocking programme targeting people in the Lango, Acholi and Teso sub-regions whose livestock was lost during the insurgency.</p><p>The government earmarked funds to compensate verified beneficiaries for cattle, goats, sheep and pigs lost during the insurgency.</p><p>However, the programme has faced delays and administrative challenges, including difficulties encountered by beneficiaries in meeting documentation requirements.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/b83c00243250050b.jpg', 'Community members  meeting at Alito Town Council headquarters on Monday  17th August 2026 to scrutinize  issue  concerning PDM', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 79, '2026-08-18 10:23:12', '2026-09-02 18:39:13', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(50, '86 Applicants from Pader and Agago Qualify in 2026 UPDF Recruitment Exercise', '86-applicants-from-pader-and-agago-qualify-in-2026-updf-recruitment-exercise', 'By Regina Lalam PADER DISTRICT - A total of 86 applicants from Pader and Agago districts have successfully qualified in the 2026 Uganda People’s Defence Forces…', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>PADER DISTRICT -</strong> A total of 86 applicants from Pader and Agago districts have successfully qualified in the 2026 Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) recruitment exercise for the Agago-Pader .</p><p>According to official results released at the end of the screening, 42 applicants from Pader District and 44 from Agago District met the required standards and have been cleared to proceed to the next stage of recruitment.</p><p>The exercise was conducted at Pader District Headquarters and attracted hundreds of youth from both districts who turned up to compete for slots in the national army.</p><p>UPDF recruitment officials noted that the process was carried out transparently and in line with the force’s guidelines on age, medical fitness, education, and discipline.</p><p>The successful candidates from the Pader-Agago cluster will now join other qualified recruits from across the country as the UPDF continues with its nationwide enlistment drive for 2026.</p><p>The recruitment exercise is part of UPDF’s ongoing efforts to bolster troop numbers and bring in new, disciplined personnel* to serve in different capacities within the force.</p><p>Local leaders in both Pader and Agago congratulated the successful applicants and urged them to remain disciplined and patriotic as they prepare to serve the nation.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/11c5f582974f7a21.jpg', 'UPDF recruitment in Pader District Head Quarters Starts with Screening exercise', 1, 1, NULL, 'The exercise was conducted at Pader District Headquarters and attracted hundreds of youth from both districts who turned up to compete for slots in the national army.', 'published', 1, 80, '2026-08-18 11:25:10', '2026-09-02 07:37:00', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(51, 'Government Responds to Food Crisis in Agago as Pastor Kakande Donates 20 Metric Tonnes of Maize Flour', 'government-responds-to-food-crisis-in-agago-as-pastor-kakande-donates-20-metric-tonnes-of-maize-flour', 'Minister Sam Engola led a government delegation to Agago District, delivering crucial food aid to households facing severe food insecurity.', '<p><span>The Government of Uganda has stepped up its response to the hunger crisis in </span><strong>Agago District</strong><span>, with the dispatch of emergency food relief to communities facing severe food insecurity.</span></p><p><span>This intervention was boosted by a generous donation of </span><strong>twenty metric tonnes of Maize flour</strong><span> from </span><strong>Pastor Samuel Kakande</strong><span> of the Synagogue Church of All Nations. The food was handed over to the Rt. Hon. Prime Minister, </span><strong>Robinah Nabbanja</strong><span>, at the Office of the Prime Minister headquarters in Kampala this morning.</span></p><p><span>The Prime Minister was joined by Ministers responsible for Disasters, Northern Uganda, Karamoja Affairs, Teso Affairs, Bunyoro Affairs, and Luwero Triangle Affairs in receiving the donation. They appreciated Pastor Kakande for his timely contribution.</span></p><p><span>Agago District, which neighbours Kotido District in Karamoja, has been severely affected by prolonged drought, leading to poor harvests and widespread food shortages. Local leaders have raised concerns about increasing malnutrition, particularly among children and the elderly.</span></p><p><span>Speaking during the dispatch ceremony, the Minister for Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, </span><strong>Hon. Sam Engola</strong><span>, reaffirmed the Government\'s commitment to ensuring that no Ugandan goes to bed hungry. He commended Pastor Kakande Ministries for their generous donation and emphasized the importance of public-private partnerships in addressing humanitarian crises.</span></p><p><span>The Office of the Prime Minister has already delivered </span><strong>6,623 metric tonnes of food</strong><span> to the affected districts of Karamoja, including Kaabong, Kotido, Moroto, Napak, Nabilatuk, Amudat, Nakapiripirit, Karenga, and Abim. The relief supplies will now be distributed by OPM and district authorities, with priority given to the most vulnerable households—including those with children, the elderly, and persons with disabilities.</span></p><p><span>Hon. Engola assured the public that the government would maintain close monitoring to ensure that the relief food reaches intended beneficiaries without any diversion or misuse.</span></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/bc17d6f7be6f8bc9.jpeg\"></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/603427b10bee0182.jpeg\"></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/680b64dec15c5d2c.jpeg', NULL, 33, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 21, '2026-08-18 16:01:39', '2026-09-03 03:16:58', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(52, 'FUFA Hands Over Kadiba Stadium to NCS for AFCON 2027 Upgrades', 'fufa-hands-over-kadiba-stadium-to-ncs-for-afcon-2027-upgrades', 'The facility, which served as a training venue during the recently concluded African Nations Championship (CHAN), will now undergo further upgrades to meet CAF standards ahead of the continental showpiece that Uganda will co-host with Kenya and Tanzania.', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p>KAMPALA – The Federation of Uganda Football Associations (FUFA) on Tuesday officially handed over FUFA Stadium, Kadiba to the National Council of Sports (NCS) for a major pitch redevelopment, as Uganda steps up preparations to host the Africa Cup of Nations (AFCON) 2027.</p><p>The facility, which served as a training venue during the recently concluded African Nations Championship (CHAN), will now undergo further upgrades to meet CAF standards ahead of the continental showpiece that Uganda will co-host with Kenya and Tanzania.</p><p>According to FUFA, the redevelopment will focus on three key areas:</p><p>Playing surface to meet international pitch standards</p><p>Floodlights – for night matches and training</p><p> Drainage system– to ensure playability during the rainy season</p><p>The upgrades are part of Uganda’s broader plan to have world-class training venues ready to support teams during AFCON 2027.</p><p>The brief handover ceremony was witnessed by:</p><p>Hon. Peter Ogwang, Minister of State for Sports</p><p>Ambrose Tashobya, NCS Chairman  </p><p>FUFA delegation led by President Hon. Magogo Moses Hassim</p><p>Representatives from the Ministry of Works and Transportand the Ministry of Defence and Veteran Affairs</p><p>Speaking at the event, officials emphasized that the handover marks “another critical step”in ensuring Uganda’s football infrastructure is ready and compliant for Africa’s biggest football tournament.</p><p>Kadiba Stadium is one of several venues earmarked to serve as official team training bases during AFCON 2027, alongside Namboole, St. Mary’s Kitende, and Lugogo.</p><p>With works set to begin immediately, FUFA and NCS say the goal is to deliver a facility that matches CAF requirements in time for 2027.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/e4d66d21a585118f.jpg', 'Photo by FUFA', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 37, '2026-08-18 17:40:48', '2026-08-30 07:03:39', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(53, 'Marking of UCE and UACE Mock Exams Starts in Lira City with 500 Teachers', 'marking-of-uce-and-uace-mock-exams-starts-in-lira-city-with-500-teachers', 'The exercise was officially opened by Canon Jane Acio Obeny,the Lira City Education Officer,who urged teachers involved in the marking to maintain professionalism, integrity and fairness throughout the exercise.', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY  </strong>- More than 500 teachers from four regions have begun marking the 2026 UCE and UACE Mock examinations in Lira City,with the exercise taking place at Lango College.</p><p>The marking exercise,which started on Tuesday,August 18, 2026,brings together teachers from the Lango,Acholi,West Nile and another participating region to assess mock examination scripts for Senior Four and Senior Six candidates.</p><p>The exercise was officially opened by Canon Jane Acio Obeny,the Lira City Education Officer,who urged teachers involved in the marking to maintain professionalism, integrity and fairness throughout the exercise.</p><p>Canon Acio Obeny said teachers should strictly follow the marking guidelines and standards used in the Uganda Certificate of Education (UCE) and Uganda Advanced Certificate of Education (UACE) examinations.</p><p>She also encouraged the markers to apply their expertise when assessing candidates\' work,saying the mock examinations are intended to help learners understand their strengths and weaknesses before sitting their final national examinations.</p><p>According to Canon Acio Obeny,teachers should not view the marking exercise as an opportunity to undermine or discourage learners,but rather as part of the preparation process aimed at improving their academic performance.</p><p>She further cautioned teachers against compromising the marking process, emphasizing the need to uphold honesty, accuracy and professionalism.She pledged continued support and supervision of the marking exercise.</p><p>Meanwhile,Isaac Ocoo,the Lango Sub-region Chairperson for the Association of Secondary Head Teachers of Uganda (ASHU),reminded teachers that the exercise is not the official Uganda National Examinations Board (UNEB) marking process.</p><p>Ocoo said the mock examinations are part of the learners\' preparation and urged teachers to use the exercise to identify areas where candidates need additional support rather than abusing their authority during marking.</p><p>Evalin Ayugi,the Executive Secretary of the LASMEA said the marking exercise involves teachers drawn from four regions.</p><p>Ayugi said a total of 7,807 candidates are sitting for the UCE Mock examinations,while 2,296 candidates are sitting for the UACE Mock examinations across the participating regions.</p><p>The marking exercise at Lango College is expected to continue for ten days,after which the results will help schools and teachers identify areas requiring improvement ahead of the national UCE and UACE examinations.</p><p>The exercise is part of efforts by schools and education stakeholders to strengthen candidates\' preparedness,improve academic performance and familiarize learners with examination standards before they sit their final national examinations.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/ed99dd80f3280160.jpg', 'Teachers from the four sub regions of  Lango, Acholi West Nile are set to mark UCE &UACE Mock papers', 10, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 78, '2026-08-18 22:44:49', '2026-09-03 04:55:42', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(54, 'MPs Commit Funding for Self-Care Programs After Health Ministry Orientation', 'mps-commit-funding-for-self-care-programs-after-health-ministry-orientation', 'Health officials told MPs that self-care is gaining global attention for its role in empowering individuals, families, and communities to take charge of their health.', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>KAMPALA – </strong>Members of the 12th Parliament have pledged to appropriate funds to support self-care promotion in Uganda, following an orientation conducted by the Ministry of Health (@MinofHealthUG) and the Parliamentary Forum on Maternal Health (NAWMP).</p><p>The seminar, held on Monday 17th August 2026 at Mestil Hotel in Kampala, focused on self-care for social transformation and its role in strengthening Uganda’s health system.</p><p>Health officials told MPs that self-care is gaining global attention for its role in empowering individuals, families, and communities to take charge of their health. </p><p>Key areas highlighted include  Preventing and managing non-communicable diseases, promoting clean and healthy environments, and reducing the burden on health facilities.</p><p>The Ministry of Health noted that integrating self-care into national health programs can help Ugandans manage common conditions at home while seeking professional care when needed.</p><p>MPs who attended the orientation committed to support budget allocations for self-care initiatives in partnership with the Ministry of Health and other stakeholders including @cehurduganda ,Dr. Charles Ayume (@DrAyumeCharles) and members of NAWMP emphasized that Parliament has a critical role in creating policies and funding mechanisms that enable communities to practice safe and effective self-care.</p><p>The forum also called for increased public awareness so that Ugandans can make informed decisions about their health and wellbeing.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/1ba1ca0a79db2d5e.jpg', 'MPs Attended the health seminar on Monday 17th August 2026', 9, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 66, '2026-08-18 23:45:07', '2026-09-03 06:31:12', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(55, 'Victory Outreach Church Steps In to Support Food-Insecure Households in Karamoja.', 'victory-outreach-church-steps-in-to-support-food-insecure-households-in-karamoja', 'The assistance comes despite the government’s ongoing efforts to distribute relief food to communities affected by hunger in Karamoja. Local leaders say the amount of food reaching households remains insufficient compared with the number of people in need.', '<p>By Isaac Erick Odongo </p><p><strong>KOTIDO, Uganda —</strong> As hunger continues to affect communities across Karamoja, Victory Outreach ministryhas stepped in to provide food assistance to vulnerable households in Kotido Municipality and surrounding areas.</p><p>The church has distributed food to 500 heads of households in Kotido Municipality, saying the intervention is aimed at supporting families struggling to cope with persistent food shortages.</p><p>The assistance comes despite the government’s ongoing efforts to distribute relief food to communities affected by hunger in Karamoja. Local leaders say the amount of food reaching households remains insufficient compared with the number of people in need.</p><p>Kotido District Chief Administrative officer Emmanuel Oyuku Ocen said that while government food distributions are taking place, the supplies are not enough to meet the needs of the growing number of food-insecure households.</p><p>He attributed part of the challenge to changes in population figures used for planning and distribution, noting that some households may not have  been adequately captured in official assessments.</p><p>The situation has prompted faith-based organisations such as Victory Outreach Ministry to complement government efforts by reaching families they say are in urgent need of food.</p><p>The church’s leader, Rev. Johnson Ogema, said the ministry distributed food to vulnerable households after witnessing the difficult conditions facing communities in Karamoja.</p><p>Ogema also appealed for prayers for Karamoja, particularly for adequate rainfall and improved agricultural conditions. He urged communities to remain resilient and continue working to overcome hunger and poverty.</p><p>Paul Lotee Komol, Kotido district chairperson welcomed the church’s intervention and appealed for more organisations to support hunger-affected communities.</p><p>Lotee said the food provided by the government does not reach everyone in need, leaving some households without adequate supplies.</p><p>He called on victory outreach churche and other organisations to increase their support to communities facing severe food shortages.</p><p>The latest church intervention included 20-kilogram bags of maize flour and 10-kilogram packagesm of  beans distributed to households in Nakapelimoru and Longaroe in Kotido District.</p><p>The intervention comes as the government continues implementing measures to address hunger in Karamoja.</p><p>President Yoweri Kaguta Museveni allocated about UGX 45 billion for food distribution to hunger-affected communities, but local leaders say the scale of need remains high.</p><p>With food insecurity continuing to affect households across the region, community leaders are calling for sustained support from both government and non-governmental actors, alongside longer-term measures to strengthen food production and household resilience.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/13bf719e82ab1022.jpg', 'Beneficiaries  Receiving their food relief', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 48, '2026-08-19 09:24:19', '2026-09-03 04:55:32', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(56, 'Uganda Government and Windle International Discuss Enhanced Support for Refugees and Host Communities', 'uganda-government-and-windle-international-discuss-enhanced-support-for-refugees-and-host-communities', 'Minister Sam Engola met with Windle International Uganda to explore strengthening education and youth empowerment for refugees and host communities.', '<p class=\"ai-source-note\"><em>This article is based on reporting by <a href=\"https://skikadailynews.com/2026/08/20/engola-windle-explore-new-opportunities-for-refugees-host-communities/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Skika Daily News</a>.</em></p><h3>Ministerial Engagement on Refugee and Host Community Support</h3>\n<p>Minister of Relief, Disaster Preparedness and Refugees, Sam Engola, convened with a delegation from Windle International Uganda to discuss enhancing educational and youth empowerment initiatives. The meeting, held on Thursday, August 20, 2026, focused on creating better opportunities for both refugees and the communities hosting them.</p>\n\n<h3>Focus on Education and Skills Development</h3>\n<p>The discussions centered on broadening access to quality education, fostering skills development, and improving employment prospects for young individuals. Minister Engola acknowledged Windle International Uganda\'s long-standing contribution to education programs for refugees and host communities since 1996.</p>\n\n<h3>Windle\'s Extensive Support Network</h3>\n<p>Currently, Windle International Uganda supports 69 schools across the West Nile and Karamoja sub-regions. Their initiatives include school feeding programs and agricultural projects designed to boost school attendance and enhance local food security. The organization also actively works to combat youth unemployment in West Nile, Western Uganda, and Greater Kampala through skills training, scholarships, and job placement assistance.</p>\n\n<h3>Commitment to Partnership and Inclusive Development</h3>\n<p>Andrew Omara, Executive Director of Windle International Uganda, expressed the organization\'s dedication to strengthening pathways from education and skills training to economic opportunities. Both parties affirmed their commitment to fostering partnerships that expand opportunities for young people, build resilient communities, and contribute to an inclusive Uganda.</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 0, 0, '2026-08-20 15:21:30', '2026-08-20 12:21:30', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(57, 'Judith Alyek rejects Okwerodot women’s council election results, cites intimidation', 'judith-alyek-rejects-okwerodot-women-s-council-election-results-cites-intimidation', 'Following the rescheduled vote, Election Officer Paul Awany declared independent candidate Betty Atim the winner for the 2026–2031 term, recording 21 votes against 19 votes for Judith Alyek. Awany noted that any candidate dissatisfied with the declared results may file a petition to the returning authority for formal review.', '<p><strong>OKWERODOT, KOLE —</strong> Former Kole District Woman Member of Parliament Judith Alyek has rejected the election outcome for the Okwerodot Sub-county Women’s Council Chairperson seat.</p><p>The election followed a postponement caused by confusion over voter attire and election guidelines. On polling day, some voters arrived wearing pink outfits—a color linked to specific political affiliations—which violated regulations against partisan dress at voting centers. The election official subsequently rescheduled the poll.</p><p>Following the rescheduled vote, Election Officer Paul Awany declared independent candidate Betty Atim the winner for the 2026–2031 term, recording 21 votes against 19 votes for Judith Alyek. Awany noted that any candidate dissatisfied with the declared results may file a petition to the returning authority for formal review.</p><p>In statements to journalists, Alyek—contesting as the official National Resistance Movement (NRM) flagbearer—alleged voter intimidation and procedural irregularities during the voting and tallying process. She stated that she has documented her complaints and formally notified local police and security leadership.</p><p>Alyek also expressed disappointment with senior district leaders, accusing Kole North MP Dr. Samuel Opio Acuti, Kole Woman MP Sandra Acheng, and Kole Resident District Commissioner (RDC) Gillian Akullo of actively opposing her candidacy and supporting an independent contender against party directives.</p><p>Responding to the allegations, Kole RDC Gillian </p><p>Akullo dismissed the claims as political gamesmanship, stating she was absent during the earlier exercise due to illness and urged candidate leaders to respect the democratic process. Repeated attempts to reach Dr. Opio Acuti and Sandra Acheng for comments were unsuccessful.</p><p>Following her declaration, Betty Atim welcomed the results and expressed her commitment to serve all women in Okwerodot Sub-county regardless of political alignment.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/420b880ad0e17e31.jpg', 'Profile photo of Former MP Kole District Judith Alyek', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 14, '2026-08-20 20:00:05', '2026-08-30 00:11:53', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(58, 'Gulu City to Host Over 250 Security Personnel for Inter-Forces Sports Competition', 'gulu-city-to-host-over-250-security-personnel-for-inter-forces-sports-competition', 'By Hillary Opio Omara &amp; Regina Lalam GULU NORTHERN UGANDA - More than 250 security personnel from across Northern Uganda are set to participate in interfac…', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara &amp; Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>GULU NORTHERN UGANDA -</strong> More than 250 security personnel from across Northern Uganda are set to participate in interface sports matches in Gulu City from August 24 to September 4, 2026.</p><p>The games,organized by the 4th Infantry Division of the Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) for the Acholi Sub-region and West Nile,will bring together personnel from the UPDF,Uganda Police Force,Uganda Prisons Service and Uganda Wildlife Authority.</p><p>According to 4th Infantry Division spokesperson Maj.Bilal Katamba,the initiative is aimed at strengthening cooperation and teamwork among security agencies through sports.</p><p>The competitions will include athletics, football,netball,volleyball,handball and taekwondo,with the matches taking place at St.Joseph Layibi College in Gulu City.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c462018812ddefcd.jpg\"></p><p> <strong><em>Maj Katamba on the the  upcoming Sports competition </em></strong></p><p>Maj.Katamba said the games are part of efforts to improve the physical fitness and professional effectiveness of security personnel,while also providing an opportunity for officers from different institutions to interact and build stronger working relationships.</p><p>He said the annual sporting activities are also intended to strengthen the capacity of security personnel to remain physically fit and ready to respond to their duties at all times.</p><p>Beyond physical fitness,Maj.Katamba noted that the games will promote cooperation and friendship among the UPDF,Police, Prisons Service and Uganda Wildlife Authority,whose personnel often work together in different parts of the country.</p><p>He added that sports can also help reduce stress among security personnel,who operate under demanding conditions and are frequently deployed in different parts of the country.</p><p>Maj.Katamba told Radio Q FM that members of the public interested in watching the matches will be allowed to attend free of charge.</p><p>The interface games are expected to run for nearly two weeks,bringing together security personnel from the four institutions in a sporting event aimed at promoting fitness, teamwork,unity and stronger inter-agency relations.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/27dbd15d838af4ea.jpg', NULL, 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 72, '2026-08-20 22:27:10', '2026-09-02 12:45:42', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(59, 'UPDF 2026 Recruitment Marred by Low Turnout, Info Mismatch as Koboko and Kamwenge Fall Short of Targets', 'updf-2026-recruitment-marred-by-low-turnout-info-mismatch-as-koboko-and-kamwenge-fall-short-of-targets', 'By Regina Lalam NATIONAL NEWS / SECURITY - The ongoing 2026 Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) nationwide recruitment exercise has been hit by low turnout a…', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>NATIONAL NEWS / SECURITY</strong> - The ongoing 2026 Uganda People’s Defence Forces (UPDF) nationwide recruitment exercise has been hit by low turnout and mismatched personal information in several districts.</p><p><strong>In Koboko District</strong>, the exercise recorded a poor turnout despite 54 candidates being shortlisted for 58 slots, including three females.</p><p>According to UPDF Public Information Officer on Wednesday 20th August 2026 ,Lt. Wilfred Oloya, only 38 shortlisted candidates turned up for interviews. Of these, 13 were sent to court to obtain affidavits over discrepancies in their personal information such as names, dates of birth and academic documents.</p><p>Lt. Oloya said the affected candidates will only be allowed to proceed if they return within the required timeframe with the legal documents.</p><p>Meanwhile<strong>, in Kamwenge and Kitagwenda districts, </strong>the UPDF also failed to meet its recruitment target.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/70de5e32f51a9ee7.jpg\"></p><p><strong>Screening of the Applicants  ( Photo by Updf)</strong></p><p>The force had targeted 102 slots in the two districts but managed to recruit only 81 candidates, leaving a deficit of 21.</p><p>In Kamwenge, out of a target of 72, only 51 were successfully enrolled, including 17 professionals and just two females.</p><p>Kitagwenda met its target of 30 recruits, comprising 13 professionals, four females and nine males.</p><p>The recruitment exercise is ongoing across the country as UPDF seeks to enlist more personnel into the force.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/7dfb5026b856f9b4.jpg', 'Photo by Updf', 33, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 47, '2026-08-21 08:38:22', '2026-09-02 14:23:13', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(60, 'Shakira Among Elected NRM Flag Bearer for Woman Council Chairperson', 'shakira-among-elected-nrm-flag-bearer-for-woman-council-chairperson', 'By Hillary Opio Omara LIRA DISTRICT - Shakira Among has emerged as the NRM flag bearer for the Lira District Woman Council Chairperson seat after winning the p…', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara </p><p><strong>LIRA DISTRICT</strong> - Shakira Among has emerged as the NRM flag bearer for the Lira District Woman Council Chairperson seat after winning the party’s internal elections on Friday 21st August 2026.</p><p>The election,which was conducted on Friday, August 21,2026,attracted several candidates seeking to represent the National Resistance Movement (NRM) in the upcoming district-wide elections.</p><p>Speaking after the conclusion of the exercise,Lira District NRM Registrar Moses Okello said the election was successfully completed,with three candidates remaining in contention for the Woman Council Chairperson position.</p><p>Okello identified the candidates as Shakira Among as the daughter to Lira District Woman Member of Parliament Linda Agness Auma,Lucy Akoli and Nakembo Lyida.</p><p>According to Okello,Nakembo Lyida had polled three votes,while Lucy Akoli stepped out of the contest.Shakira Among subsequently secured six votes out of the 12 votes making her the NRM flag bearer for the position.</p><p>Other candidates who had expressed interest included Dorcus Amongi,who contested for treasurer,Judith Aol for secretary publicity and Salume Auma for vice chairperson.However,Okello said none of the other positions attracted competition.</p><p>Okello commended Lira District NRM leaders,including the district registrar,the party chairperson,Members of Parliament for Erute North and Erute South,the Lira District Woman MP and other party leaders, for their efforts to ensure that NRM members participated in the electoral process from the grassroots to the district level.</p><p>In her remarks after being declared the flag bearer,Shakira Among said women in Lira District had placed their confidence in her because of what she described as her proven commitment to the welfare and development of women.</p><p>Among pledged to work hard to ensure that women benefit from development programmes and promised to identify and address weaknesses within the women’s leadership structures.</p><p>She said she would focus on ensuring that women in the district are empowered and that gaps affecting their participation in development are addressed.</p><p>The final district election for the Woman Council Chairperson is scheduled for August 28,2026,while the national election for the Women’s Council leadership is expected to take place on September 2,2026.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/be429e53c442b970.jpg', 'Shakira NRM flag bearer Lira District receives her election Result', 3, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 51, '2026-08-21 22:13:58', '2026-09-02 16:35:14', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(61, 'Fake Job Scammers Impersonating Lira Hospital Doctor - Management Warns', 'fake-job-scammers-impersonating-lira-hospital-doctor-management-warns', 'By Hillary Opio Omara LIRA CITY LANGO - Management of Lira Regional Referral Hospital (LRRH) has warned members of the public about a suspected job scam involv…', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY LANGO</strong> - Management of Lira Regional Referral Hospital (LRRH) has warned members of the public about a suspected job scam involving an individual allegedly using the name of the hospital’s Senior Executive Consultant,Dr. Andrew Odur,to defraud unsuspecting job seekers.</p><p>According to the hospital,the suspect has been contacting members of the public using telephone number 0791 986 880, reportedly registered in the name of Brenda Akoli,and falsely promising employment opportunities at Lira Regional Referral Hospital in exchange for money.</p><p>The hospital management has described the actions as fraudulent and urged the public to be extremely cautious of anyone claiming to have the power to secure employment at the facility in exchange for payment.</p><p>“Management strongly warns the public to disregard any individual or person making fraudulent employment offers in the name of the hospital,” the statement said.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/68f68c818baf87f2.jpg\"></p><p><strong>LRRH Hospital Director Dr Andrew Odur </strong></p><p>The hospital has also urged anyone who encounters such cases of fraud,extortion or attempted solicitation to immediately report them to the relevant authorities.</p><p>The matter has already been reported to the Police,according to management,to facilitate investigations and the identification and arrest of the suspect for appropriate legal action.</p><p>Management further clarified that recruitment into public service positions at Lira Regional Referral Hospital is handled by the Health Service Commission,and that all genuine vacancies are formally advertised through official communication channels.</p><p>The hospital emphasized that no individual should pay money or provide personal information to anyone claiming to be recruiting on behalf of Lira Regional Referral Hospital outside the established recruitment process.</p><p>Lira Regional Referral Hospital reiterated its zero-tolerance policy towards corruption and called on the public to remain vigilant and report suspected recruitment scams to authorities.</p><p>The warning comes as job seekers continue to face risks from fraudsters who exploit the high demand for public-sector employment by falsely claiming connections to government institutions.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/1fb0f5a060dae1f6.jpg', 'Profile Photo LRRH', 9, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 38, '2026-08-22 00:12:14', '2026-09-02 23:12:09', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(62, 'Obucuun and Soroti City Wowen crowned Champions of 2nd Edition Ateker- cup of Nations.', 'by-regina-lalam-edition-held-last-year-in-2025-in-lodwar-turkana-county-kenya-in-the-inaugural-edition-uganda-s-ngora-fc-won-the-men-s-title-after-beating-kenya-s-kakuma-united-5-4-on-penalties-in-the-final-played-at-lodwar-mixed-primary-school-playground', 'The finals were graced by the Governor of Eastern Equatoria, General Louis Lobong Lojore, who was the Guest of Honour.', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/59597cac196d72c2.jpg\"></p><p>The finals were graced by the Governor of Eastern Equatoria, General Louis Lobong Lojore, who was the Guest of Honour.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/e8b978abb8429e15.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Louis Labong Lojore Guest of Honour on Cap in the middle</em></strong></p><p>Soroti City Women emerged champions of the women\'s category after a commanding performance.</p><p><strong><em>FULL TIME: Soroti City Women 2-0 Kaberamaido</em></strong></p><p>Soroti City dominated the encounter from start to finish to secure a 2-0 victory and lift the trophy.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c8ebd20822e05037.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>MEN\'S FINAL: OBUCUUN WIN 5 MILLION UGX AND TROPHY</em></strong></p><p>In the highly anticipated men\'s final, Kenya\'s Obucuun battled Kumi District in a tense encounter.</p><p>The game was cagey in the first half.</p><p><strong><em>HALF TIME: Kumi District 0-0 Obucuun</em></strong></p><p>After a goalless first half, both teams returned stronger, each finding the back of the net.</p><p>FULL TIME: <strong><em>Kumi District 1-1 Obucuun</em></strong></p><p>With the score tied at 1-1 after normal time, the winner had to be decided from the penalty spot.</p><p>In the shootouts, Obucuun showed composure and won 4-3 on penalties to be crowned champions.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/bab3b327c9f5862a.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Kenya\'s Obucuun on Blue shirts in action in a heated final 2nd Edition Atekere cup 2026</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Obucuun walked away with a trophy and a cash prize of Five Million (5,000,000) UGX </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>1ST EDITION FLASHBACK</em></strong></p><p>This year\'s tournament is the 2nd Edition. The inaugural edition held in 2025 in Lodwar, Turkana County, Kenya was won by Uganda\'s Ngora FC, who beat Kenya\'s Kakuma FC 5-4 on penalties in the final. That edition featured 26 teams from Ethiopia, Kenya, Uganda and South Sudan with the aim of uniting the Ateker communities through sports.</p><p>With this victory, Kenya\'s Obucuun and Soroti City Women (UG)have now etched their names in the history of the Ateker Cup of Nations.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/71a99dd26c11f7f9.jpg', 'Fans of Bucuunu joins their champions in the victory', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 23, '2026-08-22 19:57:37', '2026-09-01 12:35:41', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(63, 'Lango College Qualifies for Boys Schools Cricket week Nationals in Fort Portal', 'lango-college-qualifies-for-boys-schools-cricket-week-nationals-in-fort-portal', 'At the end of the city qualifiers, Lango College emerged as champions, followed by Mentor SS as runners-up.', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p><strong>LIRA — </strong>Lango College has qualified for the Boys Schools Cricket Week National Finals slated for 22nd - 29th in Fort Portal City.</p><p>The journey to nationals started with City qualifiers held in Lira where four schools took part including Comboni College, Lango College, Mentor SS and Railway Seed.</p><p>At the end of the city qualifiers, Lango College emerged as champions, followed by Mentor SS as runners-up.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/f872e6c417091dec.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>From Lira City Competition Cricket boys </em></strong></p><p>For the regional qualifiers, two schools were required from each region. However, since the Northern Region is big, it was allocated three slots for the nationals.</p><p>The regional qualifiers hosted in Gulu City attracted 7 schools ,3 from Gulu, 2 from Masindi, 1 from Arua and 1 from Lira. Mentor SS missed out due to transportation challenges for their players.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/2ce15a87c483289c.jpg\"></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c3c7fe62d50168b0.jpg\"></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/e5b4ef7f8a93cf26.jpg\"></p><p>At the regionals, Layibi College were crowned champions, Gulu High finished as runners-up, while Lango College took third place, securing qualification for the national finals.</p><p>All three schools have now qualified to represent the Northern Region at the nationals.</p><p><strong>School Lango College is in Group D</strong></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/41ba747416ba55f9.jpg\"></p><p>On Saturday 22nd August,the boys have set off for Fort Portal for the one-week long Boys Schools Cricket Week National Championship that runs from 22nd to 29th August.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/ac7cd5c482b005fa.jpg', 'Group Photo Lango College Cricket Players', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 44, '2026-08-23 01:16:35', '2026-09-01 12:35:40', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(64, 'P.1 Pupil Knocked Dead Along Soroti  Lira Highway, Driver intercepted in Amugu.', 'p-1-pupil-knocked-dead-along-soroti-lira-highway-driver-intercepted-in-amugu', 'By press time,  Police officers had arrived at the scene and recorded statements.', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p>LIRA - A Primary One child, aged between 8-10 years, has died on Sunday  morning 23rd August 2026 after being knocked by a car registration number UBM 727U along Lira-Soroti road.</p><p>According to the area Local Council One Chairperson of Agengi Bar -dyang , Mr. Adonyo Felix, who spoke from the scene on Sunday morning, the child died instantly.</p><p>Adonyo said the driver who was driving from Soroti road to Lira did not stop after knocking the child and continued driving, but was later intercepted by police in Amugu.</p><p>By press time, police from Dokolo Police Station had arrived at the scene and recorded statements.</p><p>Adonyo  confirmed the deceased is  a Primary One pupil.</p><p>More details and the official police report will follow.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/e4ac24295d241f68.jpg', 'Police officers records the incident ( accident)', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 21, '2026-08-23 15:44:24', '2026-08-31 06:09:36', 0, 1, 'inter');
INSERT INTO `articles` (`id`, `title`, `slug`, `excerpt`, `content`, `featured_image`, `featured_image_caption`, `category_id`, `author_id`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `status`, `is_featured`, `views`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `is_breaking`, `reading_time`, `body_font`) VALUES
(65, 'Lango College shines as Boys schools National Cricket week Bowls off', 'lango-college-shines-as-boys-schools-national-cricket-week-bowls-off', 'The biggest statement of the morning came at Kicwamba 2, where Lango College thrashed Kasese SS by a massive 112 runs, showing their intent for this year\'s title.', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p><strong>FORT PORTAL CITY –</strong>The 2026 Sky View Boys Schools Cricket Week got off to a thrilling start this Sunday in Fort Portal City, with five exciting encounters played across different grounds.</p><p>Lango College emerged as the standout performer of Day One with a dominant display, winning two games in a single day.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/5a7229c9c97a8cb8.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>DAY ONE 23rd /08/2026- MORNING RESULTS:</em></strong></p><p>At Nyakasura Ground, Masaka SSS beat Good Heart by 14 runs in a closely contested game to register their first win of the tournament.</p><p>At Kicwamba 1, after Jinja S.S won the toss and asked Soroti S.S to bat first, Soroti SS edged Jinja SSS by 6 runs in a nail-biting low-scoring thriller.</p><p>The biggest statement of the morning came at Kicwamba 2, where Lango College thrashed Kasese SS by a massive 112 runs, showing their intent for this year\'s title.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/e3415ff54277ac7e.jpg\"></p><p>Hosts Nyakasura School gave their home fans something to celebrate at SLECK 1, after comfortably beating St. Cornelius by 8 wickets.</p><p>Meanwhile at SLECK 2, Shree International School Kira secured a convincing 66-run victory over KC Butiiki.</p><p>In another heated afternoon encounter that started at 2PM, Lango College registered their second win of the day.</p><p>Olila High struggled with the bat, managing only 76/9 in 15 overs.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/c88ba76e27c39b03.jpg\"></p><p>Olila high School boys cricket Players</p><p>Lango College chased down the target, scoring 79/5 in 14 overs to win by 5 wickets.</p><p>With two wins from two games on Match Day One, Lango College has sent a strong warning to title contenders.</p><p>DAY ONE  ALL RESULTS  23RD 08 2026</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/d1b6b65ec1fc773a.jpg\"></p><p>The action continues on Monday with more mouth-watering group games as schools battle for quarterfinal slots.</p><p><strong>Next Fixtures 24/08/2026- 10:00 AM</strong></p><p>- Lango College vs Shree SS</p><p>- Busoga High School v Gulu High School</p><p>Afternoon Fixtures - 2:00 PM</p><p>- Lango College vs Rwenzori High School</p><p>- Gulu High School vs Kira College Butiki</p><p>Other fixtures will also be played across the five venues in Fort Portal.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/ea735685212534a4.jpg', 'Cricket Boys Lango Collage on Blue and Green', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 46, '2026-08-23 23:01:36', '2026-09-02 10:29:41', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(66, 'Preparations Underway for National Cleaning Day', 'preparations-underway-for-national-cleaning-day', 'The Deputy Head of Public Service chaired a meeting to coordinate efforts for the upcoming National Cleaning Day.', '<h3>Coordination Meeting Held for National Cleaning Day</h3><p>Preparations are in full swing for the upcoming National Cleaning Day, scheduled to take place in four days. The Deputy Head of Public Service, Jane Mwesiga, led a coordination meeting this morning to ensure all stakeholders are aligned.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/04aa6ec322280d2d.jpeg\"></p><h3>Key Ministries and Organizations Involved.</h3><p>Representatives from various government bodies attended the crucial meeting. These included officials from the Ministry of Information, Communications, and Technology; the Uganda Media Centre; the Ministry of Health; the Kampala Capital City Authority (KCCA); and the Ministry of Local Government.</p><h3>GASP-Uganda Joins National Effort</h3><p>The meeting also welcomed GASP-Uganda, an organization that unites major manufacturers such as Uganda Breweries, Pepsi Cola, Coca-Cola, Mukwano, and Hariss International. GASP-Uganda\'s involvement is aimed at promoting effective waste management, particularly concerning packaging waste.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/40aa6d2fae21ffe5.jpeg', 'Photo Credit: OPM Media', 33, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 47, '2026-08-24 14:05:58', '2026-09-02 19:27:17', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(67, 'Gulu University Pushes for Timely Completion of Business Development Centre', 'gulu-university-pushes-for-timely-completion-of-business-development-centre', 'Gulu University management is closely monitoring the construction of its new Business Development Centre to ensure it meets deadlines, safety standards, and quality benchmarks.', '<p><em>This article is based on reporting by <a href=\"https://x.com/GuluVarsity/status/2091818122743308590\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Gulu University</a>.</em></p><h2>University Management Reviews Construction Progress</h2><p>Gulu University\'s leadership, under the guidance of Vice Chancellor Prof. George Ladaah Openjuru, is actively overseeing the construction of the new Business Development Centre. The aim is to guarantee the project\'s timely completion, adherence to safety protocols, and overall quality of work.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/44185ee0ed195a59.jpeg\"></p><h3>Collaborative Assessment Held</h3><p>A recent assessment meeting brought together key stakeholders, including top management, student leaders, the Emergency Management Team (EMT), the contractor, and supervisors. This collaborative effort focused on developing strategies to expedite the construction process and ensure the facility is ready as soon as possible.</p><h3>Addressing Infrastructure Needs</h3><p>Deputy Vice Chancellor Prof. Davy David Okello Owiny highlighted the critical need for the new centre, stating it will alleviate pressure on existing university infrastructure. The growing student population necessitates additional space to accommodate academic and administrative activities, thereby improving service delivery and the learning environment.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/be5b00cfcd504cef.jpeg\"></p><h3>Canteen Facility to Open Soon</h3><p>In addition to the main centre, the contractor has committed to completing the canteen space by October 10th. This will provide immediate convenience for students and staff upon the facility\'s opening, offering a much-needed amenity.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/eef0c0df1093c0c3.jpeg\"></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/ed23d0e2ca7fe747.jpeg', 'Photo Credit: Gulu University', 10, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 31, '2026-08-24 15:51:30', '2026-09-02 18:39:17', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(68, 'Man ,25, Lyched after allaged burglary in Lira City', 'man-25-lyched-after-allaged-burglary-in-lira-city', 'The deceased has been identified as Alany Gerald, 25, a self-employed resident of Obutuwelo A Cell, Ojwina Ward C, Lira City West Division.', '<p>BY Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY</strong> -Police in Lira City West Division are investigating a case of suspected murder by mob that claimed the life of a 25-year-old man.</p><p>The deceased has been identified as Alany Gerald, 25, a self-employed resident of Obutuwelo A Cell, Ojwina Ward C, Lira City West Division.</p><p>According to preliminary police findings, the incident happened in the night of August 24, 2026, at unknown hours. It is alleged that Alany and others still at large broke into a yet-to-be-identified home in Obutuwelo A Cell while occupants were sleeping and stole household items.</p><p>Police say the group allegedly returned to the same home to steal more items, but Alany was arrested by the homeowner while his colleagues escaped.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/620d7544a967cbb1.jpg\"></p><p><strong>Sign Post Lira City West division </strong></p><p>He was beaten by the family members before other community members joined and killed him instantly. His body was later dumped in the middle of the road.</p><p>The case was reported to police by a concerned citizen. A team of officers led by the OC Station, with SOCO and homicide detectives, responded to the scene, processed and documented it, and recorded relevant statements.</p><p>The body was retrieved and conveyed to Lira Regional Referral Hospital mortuary pending post-mortem examination.</p><p>No arrest has been made yet, but efforts to apprehend suspects are ongoing.</p><p>Police have condemned the act of mob justice, appealing to the public to desist from taking the law into their own hands and instead apprehend suspects and hand them over for investigation and prosecution.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/196079e88f03bb16.jpg', 'Profile Photo yellow tap for crime scene', 2, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 55, '2026-08-25 16:49:16', '2026-09-03 02:18:32', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(69, 'Kole MP North Urges Museveni to Reconsider Lango Roads.', 'kole-mp-north-urges-museveni-to-reconsider-lango-roads', 'By Issac Erick Odongo KOLE, UGANDA — Kole North County Member of Parliament Dr Samuel Opio Acuti has appealed to President Yoweri Kaguta Museveni to intervene …', '<p>By Issac Erick Odongo </p><p><strong><em>KOLE, UGANDA</em></strong><em> </em>— Kole North County Member of </p><p>Parliament Dr Samuel Opio Acuti has appealed to President Yoweri Kaguta Museveni to intervene and include the Corner Ayer–Aboke–Iceme–Bobi road in the government’s planned road rehabilitation programme ahead of the 2027 Africa Cup of Nations (AFCON).</p><p>The approximately 55-kilometre road is not among the routes currently identified for rehabilitation, despite its strategic importance to communities in Kole and the wider Lango sub-region, according to Opio.</p><p>In a letter dated August 21, 2026, addressed to President Museveni, the legislator urged the President to reconsider the list of roads proposed for rehabilitation and add the Lango route.</p><p>Opio said the matter was raised during President Museveni’s engagement with newly elected Members of Parliament at Kyankwanzi, where MPs presented issues requiring government intervention.</p><p>The MP argued that rehabilitating the road would improve connectivity within Lango and provide an important alternative route for players travelling from Gulu Airfield to Akii-Bua Stadium, which is expected to be one of the key venues associated with Uganda’s preparations for AFCON.</p><p>His appeal follows the Ministry of Works and Transport’s opening of bids for road rehabilitation projects, with Opio noting that none of the roads in Lango were included on the list of proposed routes, apart from the road connecting Namboole Stadium and Hoima Stadium.</p><p>Opio said he had also received reports that President Museveni had obtained an authorisation letter from the Ministry of Finance to approve funding for road works in Lango.</p><p>He cited the Namboole and Hoima roads, which he said have a combined length of about 72.2 kilometres, compared with the approximately 55-kilometre Corner Ayer–Aboke–Iceme–Bobi road.</p><p>Opio questioned why the shorter Lango route should be excluded if road length is being considered when selecting projects for rehabilitation.</p><p>The appeal comes months after the 2026 elections, in which President Museveni reportedly secured more than 80 percent of the vote in the Lango sub-region.</p><p>Opio is now urging the President to review the proposed road rehabilitation list and direct that the Corner Ayer–Aboke–Iceme–Bobi road be included among the projects to be undertaken ahead of AFCON.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/f35a53fe97ef06c2.jpg', 'MP Kole North county', 1, 1, NULL, 'In a letter dated August 21, 2026, addressed to President Museveni, the legislator urged the President to reconsider the list of roads proposed for rehabilitation and add the Lango route.', 'published', 1, 57, '2026-08-25 18:18:39', '2026-09-02 11:34:12', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(70, 'Man Found Dead in Awiodyek Swamp, Police Investigate Murder by Assault', 'man-found-dead-in-awiodyek-swamp-police-investigate-murder-by-assault', 'No arrest has been made yet, but intelligence is on the ground to identify and arrest suspects.', '<p><strong>By Regina Lalam </strong></p><p><strong>LIRA DISTRICT: </strong>Police in Lira District are investigating a suspected case of murder by assault that occurred on 22nd August 2026 at Awiodyek swamp in Awiodyek B Village, Awiodyek Parish, Awiodyek Sub-County.</p><p>The case was formally registered on 25th August 2026 at 11:58am by Okello Walter, 26, from the same village.</p><p>The deceased has been identified as Ongenyo Tonny, 44, a resident of the same area.</p><p>Preliminary findings indicate that on 22nd August at around 8:00pm, Ongenyo parked his motorcycle at home and left on foot for the nearby trading centre but never returned. His relatives searched for him the next day in vain.</p><p>On 25th August, his biological son reported a disappearance case at Wiodyek Sub-County Police Station. Later that day at around 1:00pm, while taking cows for water at Awiodyek swamp with his brother, they noticed a foul smell and discovered their father\'s body lying naked and decomposing, with his short and trouseron his face and his shirt on nearby grass.</p><p>Police from Wiodyek Sub-County and Lira District CPS led by OC CID visited and documented the scene. Statements have been recorded from witnesses and the body has been conveyed to Lira Regional Referral Hospital mortuary pending postmortem.</p><p>No arrest has been made yet, but intelligence is on the ground to identify and arrest suspects.</p><p>Police have described the incident as unfortunate and called for calm, urging community members to seek peaceful means of resolving conflicts rather than taking the law into their own hands.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/1cd4fd0623ce9d71.jpg', 'Exhibits recorded by Police', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 148, '2026-08-26 14:14:30', '2026-09-03 02:29:03', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(71, '42 Arrested in Lira City Night Operation', '42-arrested-in-lira-city-night-operation', 'The operation targeted crime hotspots in Te-Alok, Atego Ward, Starch Factory and Tekulu Ojwina, where thugs have been hiding after terrorizing residents.', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>LIRA CITY</strong> - Police in Lira City Central Police Station have arrested 42 suspects in an intelligence-led disruptive operation conducted from the night of 25th to morning of 26th August 2026.</p><p>The operation targeted crime hotspots in Te-Alok, Atego Ward, Starch Factory and Tekulu Ojwina, where thugs have been hiding after terrorizing residents.</p><p>According to Police, there has been public outcry over rising cases of housebreaking, simple robbery and phone snatching in the areas.</p><p>During the operation, exhibits including opium, pangas, a four-head spear, aviation fuel and knives were recovered.</p><p>All suspects are currently detained at Lira City Central Police Station pending joint screening with local leaders. After screening, files will be submitted to the Resident Chief State Attorney for legal guidance before they are arraigned in court.</p><p>Police have called for continued information sharing from the public and pledged commitment to ensuring a crime-free society, noting that operations will extend to other areas.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/71e21e706722d45b.jpg', 'Suspects Arrested during Night Operation', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 56, '2026-08-26 15:06:32', '2026-09-02 19:36:45', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(72, '17 Clubs Confirmed for Northern Novice Boxing Championship in Gulu', '17-clubs-confirmed-for-northern-novice-boxing-championship-in-gulu', 'By Regina Lalam GULU NORTHERN - The Northern Regional Novice Boxing Championships 2026 is set for Gulu City with 17 clubs now confirming participation.The conf…', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p>GULU NORTHERN - The Northern Regional Novice Boxing Championships 2026 is set for Gulu City with 17 clubs now confirming participation.</p><p>The confirmed clubs are Nwoya BC, Alepton BC, Pece BC, Lira City BC, Gulu BC, Arua City BC, Opeta BC, Taks BC, Nuba BC, Katrini BC, Pece Korgar BC-Omoro, Arua BC, Unique BC-Kitgum, Laliya Power House BC, Lira Destiny BC, Lacor Paradise BC and Padi BC.</p><p>Speaking to our sports desk, the Chairman Boxing Northern Region Denis Mulidra said the delay in confirming the date was because they were waiting to meet the Central Executive members from  Uganda Boxing Federation who came and met them on Wednesday and confirmed the date as required.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/9bda45ee4dc033a4.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Profile Photo for Denis Mulidra Chairman Northern Region Boxing Association </em></strong></p><p>According to the new program, the championship will start with an official weighing on Friday 5th September 2026 at 7:30am at Gulu Community Park, while the main boxing action will be on Sunday 7th September 2026.</p><p>The championship is expected to attract hundreds of fans as young boxers battle for regional glory.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/b6647868dc095b5b.jpg', 'Catersey Photo:Boxing Ring Gulu', 5, 1, NULL, 'According to the new program, the championship will start with an official weighing on Friday 5th September 2026 at 7:30am at Gulu Community Park, while the main boxing action will be on Sunday 7th September 2026.', 'published', 1, 48, '2026-08-26 21:29:50', '2026-09-02 21:50:41', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(73, 'Jeroma Probes Profit Paradox Facing Northern Uganda Farmers', 'jeroma-probes-profit-paradox-facing-northern-uganda-farmers', 'The investigation seeks to establish why farmers continue to record losses after producing quality food crops,with the company identifying poor market access, low prices,weak post-harvest handling, drought ,inadequate quality control and limited participation in cooperatives among the major challenges affecting farmers.', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara &amp; Regina Lalam</p><p><strong>LIRA CITY LANGO- </strong>The Company of Jeroma,in partnership with Access for Innovation,has launched an investigation into the factors affecting farmers in Northern Uganda,particularly the Lango Sub-region,from benefiting fully from quality agricultural produce despite producing crops on a large scale.</p><p>The investigation seeks to establish why farmers continue to record losses after producing quality food crops,with the company identifying poor market access, low prices,weak post-harvest handling, drought ,inadequate quality control and limited participation in cooperatives among the major challenges affecting farmers.</p><p>Speaking during a two day meeting organised by the Company of Jeroma in partnership with Access for Innovation at Margarita Palace Hotel in Lira City on Wednesday,August 26,2026,Sam Acuti,the Manager of the Company of Jeroma in Lira City,said the company had conducted research to understand why farmers in Northern Uganda,especially Lango,are not earning sufficient returns from their agricultural produce.</p><p>Photo by Hillary Opio Omara</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/48bccf751807a782.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Sam Acuti Company\'s Manager Jeroma</em></strong></p><p>Acuti said the findings showed that farmers are producing food crops in large quantities, but many are unable to secure profitable markets.</p><p>He attributed the losses to several factors, including farmers selling their produce at very low prices,poor-quality produce reaching markets,challenges in supplying produces outside Uganda such as South Sudan,the Democratic Republic of Congo and Kenya,poor post-harvest handling,and the limited involvement of farmers in cooperatives.</p><p>According to Acuti,the Company of Jeroma now intends to strengthen the purchase of agricultural produce from farmers at better prices while working through cooperatives to create a more reliable market for their produce.</p><p>He said the company is targeting about 14 cooperatives across Lango and Northern Uganda as part of efforts to organise farmers,improve aggregation and strengthen their bargaining power in the market.</p><p>Meanwhile,Victoria Kokunda,who works with the Company of Jeroma,said the company is also partnering with Access for Innovation to promote the use of fertilisers that can improve soil productivity and help farmers increase yields.</p><p>Kokunda said the fertilisers are intended to address challenges associated with declining soil fertility and reduce farmers\' reliance on low-quality agricultural inputs that may affect crop production.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/1b71841ee22a930f.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>Victoria Kokunda Staff for jeroma </em></strong></p><p>She encouraged farmers to adopt better farming practices and appropriate agricultural inputs to improve both the quantity and quality of their produce.</p><p>John Magnay,Senior Strategic Advisor at Access for Innovation,said the initiative would not stop at the meeting but would continue with practical interventions aimed at improving agricultural production and marketing in Lira and the wider region.</p><p>Magnay urged farmers organised under cooperatives to work together,saying collective action can help them maintain the quality of their produce,negotiate better prices and access larger markets.</p><p>He added that the company will build a seed-drying machine in Lira City to help farmers dry their seeds properly and improve the quality of their produce.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/4c1dbe74f86af45e.jpg\"></p><p><strong><em>John Magnay </em></strong></p><p>The engagement brought together agricultural stakeholders and farmers in Lira City,with participants discussing ways of improving agricultural production, post-harvest handling,collective marketing and access to better markets.</p><p>The initiative is expected to strengthen cooperation between farmers,cooperatives, agricultural input providers and buyers in an effort to reduce post-harvest losses and ensure that farmers in Northern Uganda earn better returns from their agricultural investments.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/3686cd9054595080.jpg', 'Members of Jeroma ( farmers Association)', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 59, '2026-08-27 10:59:00', '2026-09-03 02:50:50', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(74, 'Fufa gives 540 zakayo balls to upl clubs ahead of 2026/27 kickoff', 'fufa-gives-540-zakayo-balls-to-upl-clubs-ahead-of-2026-27-kickoff', 'The balls, worth UGX 60M, were handed over by FUFA Executive Committee Member Mr. Deo Mutabazi.', '<p>By Regina Lalam </p><p><strong>FUFA UGANDA</strong> - Ahead of the 2026/27 StarTimes Uganda Premier League season, FUFA has boosted all 18 UPL clubs with official match balls.</p><p>FUFA handed over 540 Zakayo balls - the official competition ball - with each of the 18 clubs receiving 30 balls.</p><p>The balls, worth UGX 60M, were handed over by FUFA Executive Committee Member Mr. Deo Mutabazi.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/3ac3e86fea7ee8b5.jpg\"></p><p>Deo Mutabazi hands over Zakayo ball\'s </p><p>According to FUFA, the initiative is in line with its Strategic Plan of supporting clubs with sports equipment.</p><p>This comes as the Uganda Premier League new season 2026/27 is set to kick off on 28th August with many exciting fixtures lined up on matchday one.</p><p>Clubs are now in final preparations for what promises to be a highly competitive season.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/de0727cad18c8a88.jpg', 'Zakayo footballs for UPL clubs', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 40, '2026-08-27 16:46:58', '2026-09-03 08:12:51', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(75, '25,000 vaccine doses arrive in Lira District to save cattle from Foot-and-Mouth Disease.', '25-000-vaccine-doses-arrive-in-lira-district-to-save-cattle-from-foot-and-mouth-disease', 'By Hillary Opio Omara LIRA DISTRICT- Lira District has received 25,000 doses of Foot-and-Mouth Disease (FMD) vaccine as the government intensifies efforts to c…', '<p>By Hillary Opio Omara</p><p><strong>LIRA DISTRICT- </strong>Lira District has received 25,000 doses of Foot-and-Mouth Disease (FMD) vaccine as the government intensifies efforts to control and prevent the spread of the highly contagious livestock disease.</p><p>The vaccines were handed over during a district-level sensitization meeting held on Thursday,August 27,2026,at Lira District Production Hall,where farmers and livestock stakeholders were briefed on the vaccination exercise.</p><p>Dr.Robert Ojala,an official from the Ministry of Agriculture,Animal Industry and Fisheries (MAAIF) and a veterinary specialist,said the government had allocated Lira District 25,000 doses to support the vaccination of livestock across the district.</p><p>He said the vaccination campaign will initially target more than 12,000 animals while vaccinating cow is at cost of UGX 8,000 and goat at cost of UGX 4,000.</p><p>Dr.Ojala urged farmers intending to have their animals vaccinated to pay the required vaccination fees directly through Housing Finance Bank,rather than handing money to individuals conducting the exercise.</p><p>He warned farmers against giving cash to people claiming to be veterinary vaccinators, stressing that payments should be made through the designated bank to ensure transparency and accountability.</p><p>Dr.Ojala further explained that every farmer whose livestock is vaccinated will receive a vaccination certificate indicating the number of animals vaccinated.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/2a67a3e81f275876.jpg\"></p><p>He said the certificates will be important when farmers move or sell their livestock, particularly as the government prepares to enforce regulations aimed at restricting the movement of unvaccinated animals.</p><p>Meanwhile,Lira District Veterinary Officer Anthony Ogwal said veterinary teams are ready to begin the vaccination exercise across the district.</p><p>Ogwal said the district,working with MAAIF, has started preparations to reach farmers in different areas and ensure that livestock are vaccinated as quickly as possible.</p><p>He explained that the nationwide vaccination campaign is part of government efforts to control and eventually eliminate Foot-and-Mouth Disease,which continues to threaten livestock production and farmers\' livelihoods.</p><p>Lira Resident District Commissioner Lilian Eyal also cautioned farmers against paying money directly to individuals carrying out the vaccination exercise.</p><p>Eyal urged farmers to follow the official payment procedures and cooperate with veterinary teams to ensure the campaign is implemented successfully.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/08/3f88c9f4fc87879c.jpg\"></p><p>RDC Lira District Lillian on Right and DPc</p><p>She said the government is investing resources to support livestock vaccination and called on farmers to take the exercise seriously by ensuring that their animals are vaccinated.</p><p>The current FMD vaccination campaign across Uganda began in August 2026 and is expected to run until November 2026,with another vaccination phase planned for January and February 2027 as the government steps up efforts to contain the disease nationwide.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/8f1ea519bf88269e.jpg', 'Members Attending the meeting', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 14, '2026-08-28 10:12:58', '2026-09-02 10:30:26', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(76, 'Pakistan Association in Lira Holds Blood Donation Drive', 'pakistan-association-in-lira-holds-blood-donation-drive', 'The Pakistan Association in Lira organized a voluntary blood donation drive at GB Restaurant, encouraging active public participation.', '<h3>Community Blood Drive Held in Lira City</h3><p>The Pakistan Association in Lira recently hosted a voluntary blood donation drive at GB Restaurant in Lira City. The initiative aimed to bolster blood supplies for local health facilities.</p><p>During the event, participants were urged to actively contribute to blood donation efforts. It was emphasized that voluntary donors are crucial for maintaining adequate blood stocks, which are vital for life-saving treatments, emergency care, and managing serious medical conditions.</p><p>The drive also highlighted the importance of blood donation in reducing maternal and pediatric mortality rates within the region. The organizers, the Pakistan Association in Lira, were commended for their dedication and ongoing humanitarian contributions to the Lango sub-region and Uganda.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/6567b04ac4d778ad.jpeg', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 11, '2026-08-30 16:55:03', '2026-09-03 04:40:13', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(77, 'Church Leaders at Awebada COU Gift Hon. Sam Engola a Chicken, Minister Pledges Car and Motorbike in Return', 'church-leaders-at-awebada-cou-gift-hon-sam-engola-a-chicken-minister-pledges-car-and-motorbike-in-return', '*Awebada, Lira City —* It was a moment of joy and thanksgiving at Awebada Church of Uganda, Bar Parish, this Sunday as church leaders expressed their love for …', '<p>*Awebada, Lira City —* It was a moment of joy and thanksgiving at Awebada Church of Uganda, Bar Parish, this Sunday as church leaders expressed their love for Hon. Min. Sam Engola with a special gift, and received generous pledges in return.</p><p>During the service, Mr. Oluka Obonyo Daniel, on behalf of the church, gifted Hon. Engola with a chicken as a token of appreciation for his continued fellowship and support to the church alonside other gifts like a sheep, ground nuts</p><p>In response, Hon. Engola, visibly moved by the gesture, announced a pledge to support the church\'s work. He pledged to gift Mr. Obonyo Daniel the (Oluka) with a motorbike to facilitate his work in the church, saying the love shown to him by the Christians had touched his heart. The motorbike will be delivered within two days.</p><p>In addition, Hon. Engola blessed the Parish Priest, Rev. Lawrence Opio Oyom, with a car to support his pastoral ministry. The car is expected to be delivered in two weeks.</p><p>Speaking to the congregation, Hon. Engola, who is also a businessman dealing in cars, revealed that his giving is rooted in his faith.</p><p>\"Every time I buy ten cars, I am given one car for free. I made a commitment that all those free cars will always be given to church leaders, because it is God who blesses me, and I must be a blessing to others as well,\" Engola said.</p><p>He further urged Christians not to misunderstand his generosity, noting that his giving is a personal covenant with God.</p><p>\"No one should feel bad about my donations. It is not about people, it is about me and my commitment to God,\" he added.</p><p>The congregation broke into ululation and praise as the pledges were made, thanking Hon. Engola for his continued support to the work of God in Lango and beyond.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/08/438b34228d8ca089.jpeg', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 26, '2026-08-30 17:11:05', '2026-09-02 20:31:39', 1, 1, 'inter'),
(78, 'Lira City Operation Nets 3 in Major Security Crackdown', 'lira-city-operation-nets-3-in-major-security-crackdown', 'The security operation was led by the Lira City West Division, Deputy Resident City Commissioner (RCC),Joan Apio alongside police and other security personnel.', '<p>LIRA CITY - Police and other security agencies have arrested three suspected criminals during a major security operation in Barapwo Ward, Lira City West Division.</p><p>The operation was conducted following numerous complaints from residents about rampant theft,drug abuse,robbery and other criminal activities in Apii-Pe Cell and other parts of Barapwo Ward.</p><p>The security operation was led by the Lira City West Division, Deputy Resident City Commissioner (RCC),Joan Apio alongside police and other security personnel.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/09/d843f448510ddc53.jpg\"></p><p>Exhibits recorded by Police </p><p>During the operation,security personnel raided several locations believed to be hiding suspected criminals and recovered suspected stolen property,including Marijuana and other items.</p><p>The Lira City RCC,Lawrence Egole,who was present during the operation,ordered the arrest of a suspected criminal identified as Gadafi Ocen.</p><p>Security personnel later arrested another suspect,identified as Innocent Acunge,who was allegedly found in possession of suspected stolen items.</p><p>Security officers subsequently extended their operation to Gadafi Ocen\'s residence, where they arrested a third suspect, identified as Oluk Oscar.</p><p>According to security officials,Oscar was allegedly found hiding inside a ceiling board during the raid.</p><p>Further searches at the residence reportedly led to the recovery of Marijuana,and other items.</p><p>Egole said the operation followed persistent complaints from residents accusing Gadafi Ocen and other suspects of involvement in livestock theft and other criminal activities.</p><p>He noted that this was not the first time security agencies had pursued Ocen, alleging that the suspect had previously released from police custody.</p><p>“We shall continue conducting security operations in Barapwo Ward until all those involved in criminal activities are arrested and brought to justice,” Egole said,noting that the area has experienced a high level of crime.</p><p>The Mayor of Lira City West Division, Emmanuel Ebong Opeto,said the arrest of the suspects was an important step towards restoring security in Barapwo Ward.</p><p>He alleged that criminal activities,including livestock theft and the circulation of suspected stolen property,had damaged the reputation of the area.</p><p>Residents of Apii-Pe Cell said the increasing cases of theft and livestock stealing had left them living in fear.</p><p>They appealed to security authorities to intensify patrols and consider re-establishing a police post in the area to improve security during both day and night.</p><p>The three suspects are currently in police custody as investigations into the allegations continue.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/09/24463a4fd420d7eb.jpg', 'Suspects arrested and brought before local leaders', 1, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 116, '2026-09-02 09:24:38', '2026-09-03 04:04:33', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(79, 'Blacks Power Maintain Perfect Start as Maroons Thrash Ntugasaze in UPL Action', 'blacks-power-maintain-perfect-start-as-maroons-thrash-ntugasaze-in-upl-action', 'Emmanuel Janan Okech was the hero for the hosts, scoring the only goal of the game in the 48th minute to secure all three points.', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p>UPL - Blacks Power FC continued their dream start to the Uganda Premier League season with a hard-fought 1-0 victory over Police FC at Hoima Stadium.</p><p>Emmanuel Janan Okech was the hero for the hosts, scoring the only goal of the game in the 48th minute to secure all three points.</p><p><img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/09/fdaca9a721ae4a4b.jpg\"></p><p><strong>Blacks Power FC </strong></p><p>The win means Blacks Power have now made it two wins in two games, keeping two clean sheets in the process.</p><p>They opened their campaign with a 1-0 win over Ntugasaze FC, with Andrea Noel Ogwal scoring the winner.</p><p>Police FC struggled to break down a resolute Blacks Power defence despite enjoying more possession.</p><p><strong>Elsewhere, Maroons FC thrash Ntugasaze FC 3-1 on the road.</strong></p><p>Ntugasaze got a consultation goal through Ronald Kaye in the 58th minute, but Maroons were ahead with 3 goals</p><p>Jackson Nunda inspired the winners with a brilliant first-half brace (18\', 36\') before Marvin Oshaba sealed the victory with a 55th-minute strike.</p><p><strong>Today\'s UPL Full-Time Results:</strong></p><p><strong>- Blacks Power FC 1-0 Police FC</strong></p><p><strong>- Ntugasaze FC 1-3 Maroons FC</strong></p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/09/47ef2d47e02cb8ac.jpg', 'Players Blacks Power fc Celebrate their goal', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 66, '2026-09-02 18:27:07', '2026-09-03 04:34:53', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(80, 'Over 80 Participants Attend UTF National Coaching and Referee Course in Gulu.', 'over-80-participants-attend-utf-national-coaching-and-refereeing-course-in-gulu', 'Lango is represented by two people namely Omara Geoffrey AKA  Joe7  and Omara Daniel', '<p>By Regina Lalam</p><p><strong>GULU CITY </strong>- More than 80 participants are taking part in the National Certificates Referee and Coaching Course organized in Northern Region under the Uganda Takekwondo Federation (UTF)in Gulu City.</p><p>Lango is represented by two people namely Omara Geoffrey AKA JOE 7 and Omara Daniel</p><p>Omara Geoffrey said the fewer numbers of participants from lango is attributed to financial constraints for paying the Course.<img src=\"/uploads/articles/2026/09/d6ff0c6b3167049e.jpg\"></p><p>He encouraged the people of lango to support Martial Arts</p><p>The coaching course, which started on Wednesday this week, will end on Thursday. At the end of the training, all participants will be awarded certificates.</p><p>The initiative is to professionalize and empower boxing across Uganda under the theme “Official, Professional, Development, in Uganda Takekwondo</p><p>According to the official announcement, the course has attracted each participant to a fee of 100,000 Uganda Shillings only, exclusive of accommodation and feeding.</p><p>The courses are expected to equip participants with modern officiating and coaching skills, boosting the standards of boxing in the Northern Region and Uganda at large.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/09/735c2ac2c5cf7356.jpg', 'Participants during the ongoing UTF  National Referee and Coaching Course in Gulu City', 5, 1, NULL, NULL, 'published', 1, 43, '2026-09-02 22:06:43', '2026-09-03 04:37:22', 0, 1, 'inter'),
(81, 'Sedrick Otolo - Lango Youth Pitches Northern Uganda Tech Hub Vision to President Museveni', 'lango-youth-pitches-northern-uganda-tech-hub-vision-to-president-museveni', 'A young innovator from Lango Sedrick Otolo has presented a compelling case for a regional tech hub to President Museveni, seeking support for youth development in Northern Uganda.', '<p>Sedrick Otolo, a technology enthusiast from Northern Uganda, has presented a proposal to President Yoweri Museveni for the establishment of a Regional Innovation Hub in the Lango Subregion. Otolo made the appeal during a meeting at Baralegi State Lodge in Otuke District on October 7, 2025.</p><p>For the past five years, Otolo has been advocating for a technology centre to provide young people in Lango with a dedicated space to hone and display their digital skills. The proposed hub aims to offer training, mentorship, and innovation facilities, thereby reducing the need for aspiring tech talents to travel to Kampala for resources.</p><p>His presentation garnered praise from journalists and local leaders for its boldness and focus on youth empowerment. Otolo also highlighted the importance of supporting talented youths who may not excel in English but possess significant technical capabilities, emphasizing their potential contribution to national development.</p><p>President Museveni reportedly expressed his admiration for Otolo\'s initiative, commending his forward-thinking approach. The President pledged the government\'s ongoing commitment to fostering innovation and promised a personal meeting at State House to discuss the proposal further.</p><p>Otolo is part of a broader group of young innovators in Lango working on digital literacy, mentorship programs, and community-focused technology projects. These efforts have already equipped numerous young individuals with practical ICT skills and the confidence to bring their innovative ideas to fruition.</p><p>The meeting at Baralegi is being viewed as a significant moment, underscoring the increasing recognition of young innovators in Northern Uganda and their potential impact on the country\'s science and technology landscape.</p>', 'uploads/articles/2026/09/ebe9a18ef3c629de.jpg', 'Sedrick Otolo - Young Innovator and Youth Mentor', 7, 1, NULL, NULL, 'draft', 0, 0, '2026-09-03 11:15:03', '2026-09-03 08:19:06', 0, 1, 'inter');

